{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts","id":981208,"title":"Do Lunars have any ancient Artifacts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-03T19:27:46-07:00","id":981208,"title":"Do Lunars have any ancient Artifacts?","content":"When I read descriptions of Artifacts, those from the First Age are invariably either lost, or owned and made solely by the Sidereals, Realm, and Lookshy.<br /> <br /> I find this rather strange. The implication is that Lunars took no artifacts with them into exile, and remembered nothing about how to make them. The very few unique Luanar weapons that I know of were given away to a Raksha (Death at the Root) or abandoned (Islebreaker).<br /> <br /> This makes no sense to me at all. Lunars should absolutely have their own ancient artifacts and knowledge that is preserved nowhere else. They should of course have things they took with them and kept from the First Age. They were not universally murdered, nor were they stopped by American airport security on their way to the Wyld. They are the heirs of the First Age just as much as the Sidereals. There is a distinct imbalance in power, but the idea that the Lunars have retained nothing at all bothers me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there some book that I haven't read that details all the cool First Age artifacts the Lunars kept for themselves or still know how to make?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:33:59-07:00","id":981212,"title":"","content":"This was something I always griped about. There are more Lunars then Sidereals and they have more free time to Create.<br /> <br /> Then again I was also for the Silver Faction and Lunars occasionally holding jobs in Heaven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T19:41:46-07:00","id":981220,"title":"","content":"I mean, Moonsilver's description mentions them stealing any such artifacts they find back.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T20:18:43-07:00","id":981237,"title":"","content":"Overall i don't worry overly much about it. A number of Lunars survived the Usurpation and coming ages, but less than Sidereals because they had to deal with remaking their powerbase, network of contacts and occult infrastructure from almost zero while being hunted to at least some degree by the dragon-blooded host, ambitious/amorous/attention-seeking Fae and stranger things and beings from Creation's borders, unlike the Sids - or the Deathlords - who were quite safely ensonced in their manses/palaces/mausoleums along with their bling and attendants in Yu-shan and the Underworld respectively, for at least most of the Shogunate era.<br /> <br /> No wonder then that, while there are First Age survivors for certain, they suffered much greater losses than the sidereals, each death also resulting in a scramble between those Lunars - or other beings - who might have a stake in claiming the guidance of the dead lunar's sucessor, its &quot;lost&quot; panoply, esoteric secrets or all of the above, conflict that might lead to greater strife, losses and distrust, specially among those Chosen of Luna that died multiple times through the ages, sometimes due to the intrigue of self-serving elder or spirit mentors. Triple the numbers can also mean triple the strife, without even counting details like Chimerae of varied degrees of functionality (some presumably even hidden amidst the Tattooed), the Silver Lady being far less of a directing influence than the Maidens, distracting bonds to the occasional returned Solar and so on.<br /> <br /> Yes, those wonders most certainly exist among the eldest, but the Lunars have lost just as many through the centuries, some (but not all recovered) and the degree of honesty about which of the chosen has which thought long lost artifacts can vary considerably, i would guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T01:02:25-07:00","id":981329,"title":"","content":"Well, they do have the Book of Three Circles.<br /> <br /> But yes, anything from the First Age tends to be pretty light on Lunar-influence. To be fair, with artefacts, Solars are better at crafting than Lunars, but as a more general point, Lunars are very much an afterthought in the First Age. And they didn't do much since.<br /> But that's a 2nd ed problem that hopefully will change in this edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T02:12:38-07:00","id":981356,"title":"","content":"The artifacts in the corebook are probably intended mostly for Solars, so they're mostly artifacts a Solar can find because it was lost or take from a DB he kills. An artifact that's &quot;canonically&quot; in the hands of a Lunar is probably harder to get into Solar hands in most games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Some of me humble homebrew for ex3:<br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\"><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hOOjEGyoq3owLoUwIwTfWKTffzo_udsiUTwomw7wudA/edit#\" target=\"_blank\">Artifacts for Crumple's DB homebrew</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1tI2T1Re0G8QOuoXkH7Y4PrKQxk1BPEGpbi82SpkTyIw/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Some Lintha QCs</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1O2I_2iWTCflJ36ggkDvjTeXmzFsGHKRxAi6L_Ry6g4w/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wyld Behemoth</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8838-tds","name":"TDS","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:02:16-07:00","id":981365,"title":"","content":"There are several things to keep in mind here:<br /> <br /> 1. The Lunars lost the Usurpation. They were forced to the edges of Creation, and the bulk of the treasures of the First Age were claimed by the DBs and Sidereals. So the Lunars had far, far fewer artifacts to begin with.<br /> <br /> 2. Lunars have less structure than the Sidereals and DBs. Therefore, while there <i>are</i> a few powerful artifacts held by Lunars, most people would see those as eg. &quot;an artifact held by Raksi&quot; rather than &quot;an artifact held by the Lunars.&quot;<br /> <br /> 3. This lack of structure, combined with the pressure of the Wyld Hunt, also makes it far harder for artifacts to stay in the hands of Lunars as a whole. Immediately after the Usurpation, many Lunars would have had personal panoplies of powerful First Age artifacts; however, as they were hunted down and killed, these were taken by the DBs and Sidereals or lost, and didn't get passed to the next generation.<br /> <br /> 4. Often the things that <i>did</i> get saved and remained in Lunar hands ended up in the possession of Lunar elders. While the elders would sometimes reward these to younger Lunars (or use them as incentives to control them), they lacked the rigid structure of inheritance or military order the DBs had, or the more coherent fellowship of the Sidereals. A DB or Sidereal could reasonably expect to inherit artifacts from the previous generation if they existed; assuming a Lunar artifact remained in Lunar hands at all, a new Lunar would have to negotiate with the elder who likely had it on an individual basis. Individual Lunar elders <i>might</i> respect your claim as the successor to the Exaltation, but they wouldn't face the structural pressure Sidereals and DBs do.<br /> <br /> 5. It's very hard for even the most powerful and established Lunars to handle a direct, overwhelming assault by the Sidereals and the Realm (or the Shogunate, earlier.) That kind of assault is expensive and risky, so it doesn't happen lightly, but what this means is that the most powerful world-shaking artifacts held by the Lunars would have been taken (or destroyed by the Lunars themselves, who would realize they couldn't defend them.) This is especially true for structures, manses, and anything else that a Lunar can't easily run off with - many powerful artifacts that were once in the hands of the Lunars were likely destroyed by the Lunars themselves when they were forced to retreat in the face of an overwhelming Dragon-Blooded assault.<br /> <br /> 6. In terms of making artifacts... Lunars aren't great at it to begin with, relatively speaking. They're probably the worst Celestials (it might be a toss-up between them and Sidereals, but Sidereals are ability-based and at least have a dedicated Craft tree.) And if you account for the sheer number of DB crafters, they might even fall behind the DB host as a whole. And that's <i>before</i> accounting for the fact that after the Usurpation, Lunars have lacked the resources available to DBs and Sidereals and have often been on the run, making it hard to establish a dedicated workshop or to focus on long-term projects. The good news is that those crafting charms that they do have are probably pretty good at crafting in poor circumstances, but... it's not gonna make up the difference, it just means they're not <i>utterly</i> unable to make stuff. The artifacts they make now are probably mostly simple, utilitarian things, at least in comparison to what they were able to craft when they had the resources of the First Age available to them (let alone what their Solar mates once crafted.) Of course this is a matter of degrees, and their artifacts are still strange and wonderful, but nobody's crafting the Five Metal Shrike or a Thousand-Forged Dragon from a box of scraps while on the run.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There are more Lunars then Sidereals and they have more free time to Create. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure I agree with the latter point. Sidereals have a day job, so to speak... but aside from the most powerful elders, Lunars often have to struggle to <i>survive</i>, and Sidereals (comparatively speaking) don't. A lot of Lunar time and energy is spent on hiding from, evading, or dealing with the Wyld Hunt. Even the really powerful ones generally have to either live far from civilization (which means a lot of their time and effort is spent on day-to-day things because they lack the broad infrastructure of civilization to draw on) or in secret (which means everything is harder for them because they have to hide.)<br /> <br /> A Sidereal can take a sabbatical, relax in a manse in Yu-Shan, and generally have nothing to worry about while they craft for a while. They probably can't do it too often, but they can do it. A Lunar doesn't generally have that luxury - you can't ask the Wyld Hunt for a time-out (and, in fact, working on some big project is probably an easy way to draw their attention.)<br /> <br /> Of course, this is relatively speaking again. Neither Lunars nor Sidereals have been able to craft too much over the past 1500 years - this is partially for setting reasons, since having piles of artifacts everywhere is bad for the game. But I'm dubious that Lunars actually have more time to craft than Sidereals do; a big part of the purpose of the Wyld Hunt, when it can't kill them outright, is specifically to <i>ensure</i> they don't have the time or resources for big projects like that by keeping them on the run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T03:07:21-07:00","id":981366,"title":"","content":"Yes... but a lot of Lunars are hidden out in the far Threshold, far from the Wyld Hunt. If you live next to a Bordermarch, the Wyld Hunt generally isn't a problem, especially if you're hidden. For example, it's not much of an issue for Gerd Marrow-Eater and the other Lunars who live in the Haslanti League. Nor is it much of an issue for Raksi or Ma-Ha-Suchi in the unassailable centre of their beastmen armies, or for Western Lunars who live under the sea, etc, etc.<br /> <br /> So I can see most of your arguments, but I'm not convinced by the &quot;there's no time to craft because the Wyld Hunt won't let them&quot; argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T04:40:53-07:00","id":981385,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately, the Lunar indolence problem is kinda well known and artifacts, as one of the biggest Solar THINGS, are probably going to come out of the books with ninety five percent &quot;First Age Solar Workmanship&quot; stamped on them. The intent of this is of course building up the Solar image in the books; grand builders of wondrous armaments and devices whose secrets are lost to the ages, only now to be rediscovered in the fallen age.<br /> <br /> In 2e I raged against this similarly. I made a Lunar craftswoman and banged my head against their terrible charms and made homebrew ones to craft at half the pace and equal power of a Solar with extra difficulty, since speed and minimums were the only things to affect in the 2e system.<br /> <br /> 3e, I've turned my sights to something more Lunar in nature, in my eyes. Artifacts can be stolen but workings in the deep wilderness, too remote for the dragon blooded to hold and too difficult to remove, feel more in the Lunar style to me, and indeed do what I had in mind with my craftswoman better anyway.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, the answer to the question is no; a grand total of two things in wonders of the first age were accredited to Lunar Exalted, and there was no book with much else aggrandizing them; it was an extremely low priority in 2e.<br /> <br /> Holden, in the what we know wiki, started previously that while artifact creating is not part of the planned 3e Lunar paradigm, &quot;you will be potentially able to have your lunar Tony Stark putting together armor in a cave from a box of scraps&quot;, or something to that effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:05:12-07:00","id":981391,"title":"","content":"Hmm. sounds like the Solars might have gotten less improvisational craft charms in favour of ones dedicated to projects of a more epic scope in order to leave some design space for Lunars to distinguish themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T05:29:18-07:00","id":981397,"title":"","content":"To be fair in 2ed Lunars were described as having titanic stores of artifacts ranging from dozens of warstriders to a garrisons-worth of First Age warships. <br /> <br /> The problem is that they were all held by the loot pinatas known as elders who were mostly interested in them as museum pieces. It is honestly rather annoying that the Silver Pact seems like one of the worst organizations in terms of support structure amongst the factions. Even in Magitech central (2ed) the Lunars never actually used or granted access to their treasures whereas the Fellowship, Realm, Deathlords and Malfeas all handed them out like candy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:13:42-07:00","id":981422,"title":"","content":"Does Raski and her invention of moonsilver tattoo not count as ancient ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:37:56-07:00","id":981433,"title":"","content":"The moonsilver tattoos are moderately troublesome because in 2e at least they're kind of an air-breathing mermaid. &quot;We wanted Lunars to have cool silver tattoos because we felt like cool silver tattoos were a cool unifying marker, so we invented a reason for them to all get those tattoos, they fucked up so bad in the wyld they broke their castes and needed tattoos to not fuck them up. What do the tattoos do that is cool? Mostly they just prevent you from degenerating into a shoggoth, either from your own powers or wyld exposure. If you pay for it you can have some artifacts built into your tattoos, but they're only the baseline artifacts of 2e and none of the cool magitech gizmos we're gonna drown the setting in later on.&quot;<br /> <br /> Most people, when they think 'artifact', think 'cool device that would be awesome to use' rather than 'plot thing that protects me from a problem that was pretty clearly invented so I'd have the plot thing'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 10-04-2016, 10:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:40:04-07:00","id":981438,"title":"","content":"I'm fairly certain that's supposed to be hyperbole. I mean I doubt the book means that literally every single last artifact in the first age has either been lost or taken by the realm, lookshy, or yu Shan. In fact we know this isn't true, the perfect belongs to none of those groups and he still has a first age artifact.<br /> I think it's just supposed to mean that they're super rare, and like others have already said lunars could only have so many. Only a small portion of them survived, and those that did could likely only take a few of their favorite artifacts with them. The result is that lunars probably only have so many artifacts from the first age. Of course by the same measure they've probably made plenty of artifacts of comparable power in the meantime.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3109-lionmanguy","name":"Lionmanguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:43:03-07:00","id":981439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981366#post981366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you live next to a Bordermarch, the Wyld Hunt generally isn't a problem\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Except for when it is. Mere proximity to the Wyld, absent actual immersion, does not actually occlude you from the Realm's astrologers. The sheer distances involved might give them reason to declare you a lower-priority target, but be assured, you're still a target, and discovering that you're crafting artifacts might actually give them reason to bump you up significantly.<br /> <br /> More importantly, even if it <i>did</i> hide you, you've only subtracted one obstacle from the list of potential crafting obstructions, and <i>added</i> &quot;stuff from the Wyld&quot; as another.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981366#post981366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For example, it's not much of an issue for Gerd Marrow-Eater and the other Lunars who live in the Haslanti League.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who aren't crafters (and moreover, aren't adjacent to the Wyld)\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981366#post981366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nor is it much of an issue for Raksi\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Instead, she has to busy herself with managing a city of apefolk. Also, aside from having come up with the moonsilver tattoos, once, hundreds of years ago, does she practice a craft now?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981366#post981366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or Ma-Ha-Suchi\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Also not a crafter. And instead, he has to busy himself with managing a horde of goatfolk.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Wyld Hunt would still be trouble for either of them.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981366#post981366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u2026or for Western Lunars who live under the sea, etc, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>And <i>they</i> have replaced &quot;the Wyld Hunt&quot; with &quot;the very drastic limitations inherent to working underwater&quot; on the list of potential crafting obstructions. Not to mention &quot;territorial pelagic gods&quot; and &quot;various underwater oogie-boogies.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Also, things beneath the sea still have destinies, so they can still be found, and get lured to the surface by various means, or even just cornered and bearded by Water Aspect DBs).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 10-04-2016, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T07:55:07-07:00","id":981443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aquillion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981365#post981365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are several things to keep in mind here:</div> </div> </div> </div>These are great points, but I'm finding it better for the game to suggest a serious presence of entropy in this process. That is to say, in the Old Days, things worked more or less about as Aquillion describes... but things have been getting worse for a long while, and just got EXPLOSIVELY worse in the last decade.<br /> <br /> Part of this is simply the powers-that-be taking the eye off the ball sixteen centuries later, which is pretty understandable even for near-immortals. Part of it is thinking the problem has been 'dealt with' ; the Lunar Exalted have been broken and scattered to the five winds, so it's a pragmatic and rational argument that handling them just doesn't require the attention and energy that it once did when they were unified. The tendency with things like this is to eventually start trying to do 'more with less' as the tedium and waste of world-wide enforcement becomes less of a priority when compared against other Really Important affairs of Yu-Shan and the Realm. At first, things are great, as waste and mismanagement are pruned from the Lunar-hunting infrastructure. Eventually, however, you hit bedrock.<br /> <br /> And of course the lion's share of the blame for the decaying hold the Sidereal Exalted have is on the Dragonblooded. A house in disorder cannot project force. The fall of the empire has brought new realities to the board, and some of those haven't even been properly appreciated yet. Certainly, also, the Lunar Exalted deserve some credit themselves. It's the nature of asymmetrical warfare that the state often seems to be solidly in control... until it isn't. Over two thousand years, we must imagine the great machine of the Usurpation has been degraded in several fundamental fashions, both from the loss of personnel and material.<br /> <br /> So final point, I think the world has changed a lot since the Lunar Elders were first hunted to the edge of Creation. The modern realm is probably massively over-estimated in terms of range and capability by the Lunar elite, and the reality is probably more anarchic than any Sidereal would be comfortable with. This is the collapse of the civilization that has ruled Creation for nearly sixteen centuries and something new will emerge from the ashes. I wouldn't be surprised if the 'wheel of history' turns a bit and Lunars start chasing Sidereals for a few thousand years!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:14:15-07:00","id":981449,"title":"","content":"actually... if the moon silver tattoos was more or less considered &quot;vital&quot; among the lunars and let's be honest moonsilver does not really grow on trees.<br /> And I doubt that the lunars had much opportunity to try and &quot;create&quot; more of it.<br /> What would be left as an option other than to melt down some of the larger artifacts that was brought along?<br /> <br /> That's just a theory of mine but i thought it could make sense, right?<br /> <br /> I hope i make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:25:22-07:00","id":981455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981449#post981449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">moonsilver does not really grow on trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC that's more or less exactly how you get it. Especially in the wyld. It's not very common though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:27:11-07:00","id":981457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981439#post981439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except for when it is. Mere proximity to the Wyld, absent actual immersion, does not actually occlude you from the Realm's astrologers. The sheer distances involved might give them reason to declare you a lower-priority target, but be assured, you're still a target, and discovering that you're crafting artifacts might actually give them reason to bump you up significantly.<br /> <br /> More importantly, even if it <i>did</i> hide you, you've only subtracted one obstacle from the list of potential crafting obstructions, and <i>added</i> &quot;stuff from the Wyld&quot; as another.<br /> <br /> Who aren't crafters (and moreover, aren't adjacent to the Wyld)\u2026<br /> <br /> Instead, she has to busy herself with managing a city of apefolk. Also, aside from having come up with the moonsilver tattoos, once, hundreds of years ago, does she practice a craft now?<br /> <br /> Also not a crafter. And instead, he has to busy himself with managing a horde of goatfolk.<br /> <br /> (Also, the Wyld Hunt would still be trouble for either of them.)<br /> <br /> And <i>they</i> have replaced &quot;the Wyld Hunt&quot; with &quot;the very drastic limitations inherent to working underwater&quot; on the list of potential crafting obstructions. Not to mention &quot;territorial pelagic gods&quot; and &quot;various underwater oogie-boogies.&quot;<br /> <br /> (Also, things beneath the sea still have destinies, so they can still be found, and get lured to the surface by various means, or even just cornered and bearded by Water Aspect DBs).</div> </div> </div> </div>My point about Ma-Ha-Suchi and Raksi was not that they themselves are likely to craft, but rather, that being a Lunar does not inherently mean you are on the run at all times with no time to craft. There are plenty of Lunars who are not on the run at all times, because of the sheer distance from areas of Realm control (that was my point about Bordermarches, perhaps I should have said the &quot;far, far threshold&quot;).<br /> I'm not saying that I expect there's tons of Lunar craftsmen out there, I don't, but that's more because I don't think most Lunars are terribly interested in forging large amounts of artefacts. But the occasional one? Sure. If you have the inspiration, and don't try and churn them out by rote, producing an artefact is something that, without speed-increasing charms, can still be done in a matter of months.<br /> But I don't think for most Lunars the Wyld Hunt itself is the reason why they don't craft.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:27:12-07:00","id":981458,"title":"","content":"Scarce moonsilver is a pretty cool idea. It makes sense if you think about it. The cheapest way to get artifacts is to... steal them from an enemy who has a ton of artifacts, so I'm sure most of the stuff the Lunar Exalted have currently is probably pilfered / stolen from the Realm. So they likely have a ton of jade and an oddly large representation of artifacts which are great for killing other Lunar Exalted. You'd be likely to see 10 common jade warstriders patched up before you'd see 1 moonsilver one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T08:51:03-07:00","id":981467,"title":"","content":"I think I largely agree with what Aquillion has said, and I find the point about scarce Moonsilver to be an interesting one.<br /> <br /> All that said, who said Lunars <i>don't</i> have some First Age artifacts? Your average Solar circle of PCs is likely to have some of the stuff from the back of the core book, and I think a few of those pieces are explicitly First Age. I don't see any reason Lunars can't take a few dots of artifacts as well. <br /> <br /> But the really big things? The massive artifact-manses that shook Creation? Those required infrastructure, both to produce and to maintain. The most wondrous things of the First Age are implied to be quite fragile in the 3e core book, ripping themselves apart or being sabotaged in the aftermath of the Usurpation. When the Lunars were driven to the far corners, they abandoned this infrastructure and probably blew up most of their own creations to deny them to the usurpers. <br /> <br /> Could some of them have rebuilt their infrastructure in situ? <i>Probably, </i>but it would have been damn hard work, and a Wyld Hunt could come in at any time, knock everything down, and take the precious time and resources for the Realm. No, better to stay mobile, craft smaller wonders, and commit to their <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:the-silver-plan\" target=\"_blank\">strategy of ripping down creation</a> by <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">committing to a type of barbarism and destruction</a>. Play to your strengths, hit and run. By no means a hard and fast rule, but a rule of thumb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10995-abakus","name":"Abakus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"105"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:25:17-07:00","id":981485,"title":"","content":"On a strictly 3rd note, the devs have said that Shape-shifting does not jive that well with Evocations so the question is why would they necessarily care that much about using most artifacts (which now rarely have advanced functions that are not Evocations). Most of the more complex works of artifice would also not really appeal, what is the point of a warstrider when you can become an invincible silver-plated Tyrant Lizard? Weapon-master Lunars are probably few and far between because it relies on giving up or at least handicapping your main strength rather than playing to it.<br /> <br /> I still like to think that the Lunars have quite a few ancient manses that they simply built in places that are tricky for other Exalts to reach, it still makes perfect sense that the First Age had quite a few exalts that liked the idea of secret retreats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T09:51:26-07:00","id":981499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981485#post981485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a strictly 3rd note, the devs have said that Shape-shifting does not jive that well with Evocations so the question is why would they necessarily care that much about using most artifacts (which now rarely have advanced functions that are not Evocations). Most of the more complex works of artifice would also not really appeal, what is the point of a warstrider when you can become an invincible silver-plated Tyrant Lizard? Weapon-master Lunars are probably few and far between because it relies on giving up or at least handicapping your main strength rather than playing to it..</div> </div> </div> </div>Focusing on the last sentence there, actually, what was basically said was that there would be three Lunar paths to combat. The Solar-ish 'I keep my human form and use artifacts and have evocations from them' that focuses on using charms. The Full Shapeshifting 'I turn into a tyrant lizard/other scary animal and crush you' one that focuses on animal shapeshifting. And then the Deadly Beast Transformation style, where you go werewolf on someone's ass.<br /> <br /> The conversation about evocations not working well for Lunars actually was about DBT - when a Lunar goes full werewolf, they will lose access to evocations and most artifact bonuses will become pointless, basically. Think of DBT as somewhat similar to being both GSS and the solar charm to make artifact armor that I forget the name of. You'll gain deadly beast evocations, and not need artifact weapon/armor ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11919-kittyempress","name":"KittyEmpress","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11919_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:02:06-07:00","id":981536,"title":"","content":"My complaint was less about Lunars never crafting artifacts -- though I do see that as a problem, especially if it's literally <b><i>never</i></b> -- but more that every single First Age artifact I read about, <a href=\"http://www.geocities.ws/the_incunabulum/exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">not just in the corebooks</a>, is either lost forever, or in the hands of DBs and Sidereals. Every last one. The one and only exception I recall is the Book of 3 Circles, which was found in a ruin instead of being retained during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> It's not like every last Lunar died, the way the Solars did. This means that during the Usurpation, every survivor threw down <i><b>all</b></i> their weapons and armor and tablet computers and warstriders and warships when they ran away. Leviathan threw away his weapon because he likes to pretend he has no hands, but what about all the other Elder survivors? <i><b>Why</b></i> would they do that? Or worse, that during the First Age they owned no artifacts, which would be stupid.<br /> <br /> Look at Crimson Armor of the Unseen Assassin. Wear that, and you're outside of Fate. Why would a Lunar not want to keep an artifact that does that?<br /> <br /> If the only answer is that Lunars are incapable of defending themselves or their artifacts from the Wyld Hunt, <i><b>ever</b></i>, and destroyed <i><b>all</b></i> their panoplies including the small portable artifacts to keep them out of Sidereal hands, that's just dumb.<br /> <br /> It just emphasizes the 1E-2E idea that Lunars are incapable and helpless and useless and also dumb, because &quot;dur hur barbarians.&quot; Lunars are at a big disadvantage, yes. But playing one should not consist of constantly running away from the Wyld Hunt because you're helpless and can't defend yourself. I know that's hyperbole, but bleck.<br /> <br /> <br /> Oh, and when powerful Lunars are killed, their artifacts are stolen. Unlike powerful Solars, who were all buried with their full panoplies out of fear of their ghosts. Even when they die, Solars are terrifying and Lunars are unimportant. NO. There should have been elaborate tombs of ancient Lunars who died by their mates' sides, or in the centuries after, with their lavish panoplies laid out because the DBs were terrified of their ghosts, just like the Solars. And the other Lunars absolutely should have looted some of those tombs and reclaimed the artifacts. Both Solar and Lunar tombs would be watched carefully by the Wyld Hunt, no doubt. But Lunars should have been able to loot <i><b>some</b></i>, nonetheless. Lunar PCs should get to loot their own tombs, especially after the Empress disappears.<br /> <br /> And Lunars should get military victories, too. They shouldn't lose all the time. They should be able to kill DBs and Sidereals and take <i><b>their</b></i> stuff, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981397#post981397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair in 2ed Lunars were described as having titanic stores of artifacts ranging from dozens of warstriders to a garrisons-worth of First Age warships.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would very much like to know more about this. Please elaborate! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-04-2016, 02:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T11:12:26-07:00","id":981543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981536#post981536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My complaint was less about Lunars never crafting artifacts -- though I do see that as a problem, especially if it's literally <b><i>never</i></b> -- but more that every single First Age artifact I read about, not just in the corebook, is either lost forever, or in the hands of DBs and Sidereals. The one and only exception I know is the Book of 3 Circles, which was found in a ruin instead of being retained during the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> It's not like every last Lunar died, the way the Solars did. This means that during the Usurpation, each and every survivor threw down <i><b>all</b></i> their weapons and armor and tablet computers and warstriders and warships when they ran away. Leviathan is explicitly described as throwing away his weapon. <i><b>Why</b></i> would they do that? Or worse, that during the First Age they owned no artifacts, which would be stupid.<br /> <br /> Look at Crimson Armor of the Unseen Assassin. Wear that, and you're outside of Fate. Why would a Lunar not want to keep an artifact that does that?<br /> <br /> It's nonsensical and just emphasizes the 1E-2E idea that Lunars are incapable and helpless and useless and also dumb, because &quot;dur hur barbarians.&quot; Lunars are at a big disadvantage. But playing one should not consist of being naked, armed with sticks, and constantly running away from the Wyld Hunt because you're helpless and can't defend yourself. I know that's slight hyperbole, but bleck.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would like to know more about this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Leviathen was a pack rat that didn't want to share his thirteen warstriders (including 3 ROYALS!) or his fancy First Age submarine fleet and generally treated his fully functional MOBILE FIRST AGE FORTRESS CITY as a glorified fishbowl (sorry I am touchy about Luthe).<br /> <br /> Raksi is hogging the Book of Three Circles (and drove its curator spirit crazy for the evulz) and countless other goodies in the mega-university of Sorcery including more warstriders.<br /> <br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi has another six (two royals) all of which are fully capable of shape-shifting and with stealth systems.<br /> <br /> And they do a grand total of nothing with these basically forcing the rest of the pact to either try to make stuff themselves (good luck since these guys also hog the only capable facilities) or risk the Wyld or Realm turf in search of loot... it was a bummer in 2ed and I hope that they are at least marginally more competent in 3ed .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T12:32:48-07:00","id":981611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981536#post981536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It just emphasizes the 1E-2E idea that Lunars are incapable and helpless and useless and also dumb, because &quot;dur hur barbarians.&quot; Lunars are at a big disadvantage, yes. But playing one should not consist of constantly running away from the Wyld Hunt because you're helpless and can't defend yourself. I know that's hyperbole, but bleck.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981543#post981543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they do a grand total of nothing with these basically forcing the rest of the pact to either try to make stuff themselves (good luck since these guys also hog the only capable facilities) or risk the Wyld or Realm turf in search of loot... it was a bummer in 2ed and I hope that they are at least marginally more competent in 3ed .</div> </div> </div> </div>I also think 3e needs a lot more Lunar competency, and a lot less Sidereal competency.<br /> <br /> Most of this seems to come from the natural reaction of writers to the 'archetype' of the splats. When you have one splat that's sorta Enkidu, and one splat that's sorta Xanatos Masters, obviously a tendency starts to come up to write the Xanatos splat as outsmarting everybody. Exalted went pretty overboard with this though. The Usurpation is one of the most one-sided fantasy conflicts I've ever read, and the aftermath fiction as it pertains to Lunars is essentially nonsensical.<br /> <br /> It's pretty clear (and unfortunate) the Usurpation was crafted as a narrative being about essentially Sidereal/Dragonblooded/Solar and then at the end of the process, Lunars were just sort of... tacked on and squeezed in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 10-04-2016, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T14:36:17-07:00","id":981698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981611#post981611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think 3e needs a lot more Lunar competency, and a lot less Sidereal competency.</div> </div> </div> </div>More Lunar competency and firepower.<br /> More Sidereal competency, less Sidereal firepower.<br /> <br /> Lunars should have and use First Age Artifacts. Probably quite a bit fewer than Sidereals and DBs, and maybe they're leery of deploying them for fear of losing them, and they probably don't need infrastructure and panoplies as much as other Exalted. But they should deploy them some of the time. And when an Elder like Ingosh dies, his stuff should end up in other Lunar hands.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation has to be a lopsided conflict or the setting falls apart, I think.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea that in the 1500 years since then, the Lunars have reorganized and waged a war of attrition against the Shogunate, Realm, and Sidereals, and it's had a major impact. I think that's a 3E idea? Hope to see more of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-04-2016, 08:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T15:18:15-07:00","id":981718,"title":"","content":"I'm not totally clear there is any problem here. I think the Lunars probably have a fair amount of magic mirrors and rings and crowns and armour and swords about them and magical boats stowed away in secret coves and the like. Aesthetically, I'd view them as having artefacts with more protean and wood, bone, etc. elements.<br /> <br /> I think the books may not talk about it as much as it should, but because of uninspired writers and / or the focus on barbarian heroes. I don't think there's really anything deeper than that going on.<br /> Is there anything specific in specifics that you think they're lacking that they should be talked about having? Any certain kinds of tools or treasure?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:26:16-07:00","id":981778,"title":"","content":"I don't think Lunars should be &quot;barbarian heroes.&quot; I think they should be exiled heirs of the First Age, more educated than any other group except Sidereals and Celestial gods, who live among 'barbarians' and rally 'barbarian' armies into terrifying war assets by need, not by choice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T16:29:19-07:00","id":981780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981698#post981698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More Lunar competency and firepower.<br /> More Sidereal competency, less Sidereal firepower.<br /> <br /> They should have and use First Age Artifacts. Probably quite a bit fewer than Sidereals and DBs, and maybe they're leery of deploying them for fear of losing them, but they should deploy them some of the time. And when an Elder like Ingosh dies, his stuff should end up in other Lunar hands.<br /> <br /> The Usurpation has to be a lopsided conflict or the setting falls apart, I think.<br /> <br /> But I like the idea that in the 1500 years since then, the Lunars have reorganized and waged a war of attrition against the Shogunate, Realm, and Sidereals, and it's had a major impact. I think that's a 3E idea? Hope to see more of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overstating the case of Sidereal &quot;firepower&quot;, by which I'm inferring you mean &quot;access to Artifacts&quot;, and the differential between Sidereals and Lunar Artifact access. At chargen (2e) they use the same Artifact rates as Lunars, though the explanation is slightly different (Starmetal is rare, Lunars are still on their heels after the Usurpation and Contagion). In <i>theory</i> Sidereals have access to Artifacts on account of their being some around Heaven and also being the secret masters of the Realm, but the red tape that would go into accessing such things is probably akin to a young Lunar convincing one of the packrat-elders to loan them something, so the answer either way is &quot;they have access to what the story says they do&quot;.<br /> <br /> From what I've seen so far I get the sense that 3e is if anything doubling down on this, backing it up by making individual artifacts more precious, and gating attunement bonuses and evocation access by Exalt-type. I would be very surprised if even in Heaven there were warehouses with racks of daiklaves and crates of armor anymore (outside a literal Raiders-of-the-Lost-Ark-style &quot;vault of dangerous stuff&quot; no one is allowed in). It seems more likely that each piece is in the possession of a <i>specific</i> god who probably has a personal or professional attachment to it. Even if a censor or division head or other powerful god has a trophy room with a dozen different daiklaves, borrowing one would at best be like asking to borrow a Rembrant. Which I guess is just to say that I expect if Sidereals have a demonstrable need for a particular artifact of any significance that's in Heaven's possession (in 3e), they'd need to convince (or politically lean on) a <i>curator</i> rather than <i>requisition</i> one from a <i>quartermaster.</i> Lunars are probably very similar in this regard. Abyssals and Infernals can probably count on gifts/loans from their patrons, but in that case you still only get what said patron decides you need or deserve. DBs are similar but with the added wrinkle that their artifacts would mostly be treasured heirlooms they're being entrusted with by their House, which adds another limitation on availability. Solars, for their part, don't have ANY of this as a rule, but make up for it by being unrivaled masters of Evocations and so better able to use any Artifact they manage to get their hands on, and for some with their personal mastery of Craft.<br /> <br /> On top of that, minor-wonder utilitarian artifacts (&quot;tablet computers&quot;) also seem to be becoming thin on the ground compared to 2e, and frankly I think it kind of diminishes the Exalted if they are knocking over Guild storehouses to steal their Winterbreath Jars or whatever. Yes, Sidereals probably have such things in whatever sort of Heavenly digs they have access to this edition (which I may remember hearing have been scaled back?), but when they're in the field I suspect the range is again akin to Lunars; there are some more homebody-ish Sidereals and Lunars (who also tend to be older) who accumulate more stuff, and then more mobile types who only have Artifacts that balance value with portability (e.g., a favored weapon).<br /> <br /> At least, that's been my read.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-04-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-04T21:14:20-07:00","id":981947,"title":"","content":"I am really new to Exalted (as of 3E). I got the impression from the core book that the Lunars from the way I see it would have a fair number of artifacts of the 1st age. Less the ones taken from ones killed by the Wyld Hunt. I imagined that Lunars would have artifacts that were more person or ideal to them. Gifted to them by Solars when they were around. Warstriders? Prolly not a lot. A ring that lets you know when those hunting you are in 10 miles of you, or a scarf that lets you blink in short teleports for a short while to quickly use terrain to your advantage. I think the Artifacts they would have are geared more to them or would be highly personal as gifts given to them.<br /> <br /> I believe their artifacts are things that help them personally immensely but may not have their value recognized by others who capture or come across them. If they were chosen servants or partners of Solars I can't believe that they would not have received numerous gifts from their betrothed or master. As for crafting things on their own I don't see why they couldn't. I just don't get the vibe that making things is something that is a big deal or desire for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12440-drakor","name":"drakor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12440_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"70"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T02:20:29-07:00","id":982023,"title":"","content":"Of course, if it IS true that the Lunars, who fled into the Wyld to escape the calamity of the Usurpation, do not presently have any artifacts...<br /> <br /> ... what was it in the Wyld that deprived them?<br /> <br /> What force beyond forces could extort the soul-bound treasures of the Lunar Exalted, the sacred vessels blessed by their goddess that they value above all other material things? Under what duress would they surrender these, the last mementos of a lost paradise? And why is it that none of them seem to remember the answer to this question? Why is it that none of them even <i>ask</i> it?<br /> <br /> And what will happen to your Circle when you journey deep into the sea of chaos beyond all knowledge, bearing moonsilver treasures in your hands and upon your brows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:29:01-07:00","id":982054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=981439#post981439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Instead, she has to busy herself with managing a city of apefolk. Also, aside from having come up with the moonsilver tattoos, once, hundreds of years ago, does she practice a craft now?</div> </div> </div> </div> 2e Raksi has one of my favourite artifacts created exclusively for an NPC.<br /> Her Malfean Lacquer is something she invented while studying demon essence in an unsuccessful attempt to modify her own Exaltation and learn Solar Circle Sorcery. It shows she's not been mindlessly struggling against a hard limitation for centuries like an idiot and actually reaped some reward from her failures. On a visual level it keeps her creepy double jointed fingers in focus, the fact she'd paint her nails when she knows she's going into a fight gives her a certain je ne sais quoi. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T04:54:35-07:00","id":982061,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:30:15-07:00","id":982112,"title":"","content":"For fun, let's picture Creation as a reality show.<br /> <br /> Some of the people on the show have been hanging out in the First Age for like... -3000 years-. During this time, they've lived in the lap of luxury essentially, afforded every convenience that you can imagine. They do lots of military stuff, as a general rule, so they fight lotsa battles and wars too. During this time, they enjoy training in the most sophisticated and advanced technology of that already impressive era. Over thousands of years they master and rely upon these tools to dispatch serious foes, many of which test them to the edge of ability... but good thing, they have all the wonderful toys the First Age has to offer!<br /> <br /> Now in the new season of our show, post-Usurpation, everything has changed! It's off to the Wyld for the entire cast!<br /> <br /> Imagine the hijinks that will ensue as our beloved tech-addicted cultural children of the modern first age try to wear animal skins for the first time! Can they make fire without essence lasers? How will they learn to play tribal drums without automaton servants?<br /> <br /> (The real answer, of course, is that they wouldn't. The Usurpation essentially involves taking a group of people who are the 1% of Creation... the rich and powerful... who have been natives of a highly sophisticated technology-based society... and having them just give up all that to go live in the woods because they're 'really angry/scared'. Never mind that both of those things would seem to motivate them to rely on artifacts MORE, not less...)<br /> <br /> (And let's not forget they abandon any Dragonblooded spouse/children/bestfriends... of which they likely had FAR MORE personal contact with than the Sidereal Exalted did, who were reclusive and not popular generals/warlords generally. Also because they're 'really angry/scared'.)<br /> <br /> It really is just a nonsensical story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3386,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","user":"Piff","date":". 10-05-2016, 10:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T07:50:51-07:00","id":982124,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982112#post982112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm gonna treat this entirely seriously for a second to point out how silly the Lunar-artifact paradigm is currently.<br /> <br /> Picture Creation as a reality show.<br /> <br /> Some of the people on the show have been hanging out in the First Age for like... -3000 years-. During this time, they've lived in the lap of luxury essentially, afforded every convenience that you can imagine. They do lots of military stuff, as a general rule, so they fight lotsa battles and wars too. During this time, they enjoy training in the most sophisticated and advanced technology of that already impressive era. Over thousands of years they master and rely upon these tools to dispatch serious foes, many of which test them to the edge of ability... but good thing, they have all the wonderful toys the First Age has to offer!<br /> <br /> Now in the new season of our show, post-Usurpation, everything has changed! It's off to the Wyld for the entire cast!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much in this edition. They remained close to Creation, and started changing due to the loss of the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Imagine the hijinks that will ensue as our beloved tech-addicted cultural children of the modern first age try to wear animal skins for the first time! Can they make fire without essence lasers? How will they learn to play tribal drums without automaton servants?<br /> <br /> (The real answer, of course, is that they wouldn't. The Usurpation essentially involves taking a group of people who are the 1% of Creation... the rich and powerful... who have been natives of a highly sophisticated technology-based society... and having them just give up all that to go live in the woods because they're 'really angry/scared'. Never mind that both of those things would seem to motivate them to rely on artifacts MORE, not less...) </div> </div> </div>It wasn't a tiny emotional tiff that kept them away, in any edition. It was because lots of them died. And more would have died if they had tried to rush in like Leeroy Jenkins to try and fight head to head. All of those weapons systems needed operators; the Dragon-Blooded were likely trusted with their operation, and, well, you can probably see where attempts to strike back might fail if all of your gunners decide to train their weapons on you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (And let's not forget they abandon any Dragonblooded spouse/children/bestfriends... of which they likely had FAR MORE personal contact with than the Sidereal Exalted did, who were reclusive and not popular generals/warlords generally. Also because they're 'really angry/scared'.) </div> </div> </div>The other Dragon-Blooded probably killed them in the process, so they could help exactly once, in the scene where they died. Also, more contact with Lunars could have been detrimental to their loyalty, since they were still kind of scary even back then, after they had lived with divisions of power that made them more accustomed to life in whatever kind of Kirby-esque wonderland it had been...In which they often served as the secret police for the Solars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It really is just a nonsensical story. </div> </div> </div>You're not getting to the parts the really fell apart in the past. Any kind of cordial relationship to the Fair Folk that they had been fighting during the First Age, even for a short period of time? Not fouling up the construction of the bonevangelion that the Deathlords used to break the Jade Prison? Somehow being responsible for the formation of a bunch of threshold societies even though this would be really dangerous and wasn't their forte?<br /> <br /> Fortunately, third edition actually wrote them back into what was happening in Creation, even if it wasn't the clumsy secret masterminds of 2e whose work is all going to get turned aside by the Solars five minutes after a golden Second Breath. You want those sweet weapons to use against the Terrestrials? Find one that's been passed down from mother to daughter in the Realm for generations, kill the family, and take their stuff. Just make sure to have an escape route ready.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:25:19-07:00","id":982135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982124#post982124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't a tiny emotional tiff that kept them away, in any edition. It was because lots of them died. And more would have died if they had tried to rush in like Leeroy Jenkins to try and fight head to head.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems a reason to rely MORE on established tools and training, not to abandon them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982124#post982124\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other Dragon-Blooded probably killed them in the process, so they could help exactly once, in the scene where they died. Also, more contact with Lunars could have been detrimental to their loyalty, since they were still kind of scary even back then, after they had lived with divisions of power that made them more accustomed to life in whatever kind of Kirby-esque wonderland it had been...In which they often served as the secret police for the Solars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Lunar Exalted may have had secret police amongst them, but that responsibility was primarily on the Night caste and those associated with it. According to both 1e and 2e, the Lunar Exalted were the 'Generals' of the old realm, often predisposed to military careers and in many other cases acting as regional majordomos.<br /> <br /> What I have never understood about this is the following - the Lunar Exalted had MORE Dragonblooded connections and allies in the Late First Age, not less. The books have been very consistant about portraying the Sidereal exalted as somewhat marginalized during the First Age, without a great deal of 'public relations' going on or extensive cults of personality. Beyond that, the Sidereal Exalted had another job that didn't put them into contact with the Dragonblooded Legions anywhere near as much. Meanwhile, Lunar Alexander has been securing spoils and riches for his soldiers for literally millenia. Plus, in pure numerical terms, they outnumber the Sidereal Exalted 2-1 at least. Just more faces.<br /> <br /> Why then did the Dragonblooded... who had been serving alongside the Lunar Exalted to a far greater degree than the Sidereal Exalted... suddenly betray them? These are relationships that go back centuries, between military comrades who have been to WAR alongside each other. Lunar Exalted are charismatic creatures! And heroic! Why would the Sidereal-loyal conspirators outnumber the Lunar-loyal soldiers? I get that the Solar Exalted were being monsters according to some interpretations, but why did that reflect on the Lunar Exalted suddenly and without warning?<br /> <br /> Why do the Lunar Exalted now completely eschew cultivating bloodlines of the ancestral warrior comrades they fought alongside with (with great success) for ALL OF HISTORY? And why do those bloodlines all foreswear loyalty to these mythic commanders in perpetuity, gathering up on the Realm in a big splat-based team?<br /> <br /> It would seem to me that a 'Lunar Usurpation' of sorts needs to be written, some explanation of why the Lunar Exalted ALSO were reviled and turned against beyond the very, very unsatisfying 'well they kinda got lumped in with the Solar Exalted'. I don't mind the set up as it stands but it's very poorly explained.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:33:31-07:00","id":982139,"title":"","content":"I think in previous editions this was one of the things the old Solar Bond was supposed to explain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:39:17-07:00","id":982142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982135#post982135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This seems a reason to rely MORE on established tools and training, not to abandon them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, if they had them. (They didn't.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Lunar Exalted may have had secret police amongst them, but that responsibility was primarily on the Night caste and those associated with it. According to both 1e and 2e, the Lunar Exalted were the 'Generals' of the old realm, often predisposed to military careers and in many other cases acting as regional majordomos. </div> </div> </div>In 1e, they were mentioned as living lives of ease as beasts in gardens between being let out to devour the enemies of the state. Nights were not the only secret police; they also had werewolf secret police.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What I have never understood about this is the following - the Lunar Exalted had MORE Dragonblooded connections and allies in the Late First Age, not less. The books have been very consistant about portraying the Sidereal exalted as somewhat marginalized during the First Age, without a great deal of 'public relations' going on or extensive cults of personality. Beyond that, the Sidereal Exalted had another job that didn't put them into contact with the Dragonblooded Legions anywhere near as much. Meanwhile, Lunar Alexander has been securing spoils and riches for his soldiers for literally millenia. Plus, in pure numerical terms, they outnumber the Sidereal Exalted 2-1 at least. Just more faces. </div> </div> </div>More faces that change at a moment's notice and which might very well become utterly horrifying. Besides, what if the family of the Dragon-Blooded had a member that ended up being eaten? Again, spending more time around Lunars might not translate to thinking more fondly of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why then did the Dragonblooded... who had been serving alongside the Lunar Exalted to a far greater degree than the Sidereal Exalted... suddenly betray them? These are relationships that go back centuries, between military comrades who have been to WAR alongside each other. Lunar Exalted are charismatic creatures! And heroic! Why would the Sidereal-loyal conspirators outnumber the Lunar-loyal soldiers? I get that the Solar Exalted were being monsters according to some interpretations, but why did that reflect on the Lunar Exalted suddenly and without warning? </div> </div> </div>Because the Lunars were by and large loyal to the Solars. 1e also mentioned them as going and doing in the night what Solars couldn't bring themselves to do, so it doesn't sound like there was much in the way of smiles or sunshine there, especially if some Dragon-Blooded were labeled as disloyal and ended up being devoured. At that point, the assassinated/cannibalized group becomes a pack of martyrs, and their names become rallying cries. Sidereals just have to make sure that word gets out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why do the Lunar Exalted now completely eschew cultivating bloodlines of the ancestral warrior comrades they fought alongside with (with great success) for ALL OF HISTORY? And why do those bloodlines all foreswear loyalty to these mythic commanders in perpetuity, gathering up on the Realm in a big splat-based team? </div> </div> </div>Because all of the few loyal Dragon-Blooded probably died a long time ago. Blood bats and like organizations are going to be pretty damned rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It would seem to me that a 'Lunar Usurpation' of sorts needs to be written, some explanation of why the Lunar Exalted ALSO were reviled and turned against beyond the very, very unsatisfying 'well they kinda got lumped in with the Solar Exalted'. I don't mind the set up as it stands but it's very poorly explained. </div> </div> </div>You mean aside from acting as werewolves at the behest of increasingly unhinged warlords and sorcerers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:45:33-07:00","id":982145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982139#post982139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think in previous editions this was one of the things the old Solar Bond was supposed to explain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, this all predates Solar Bond.<br /> <br /> Look, the real reason is frustratingly simple - not a lot of thought has been given to the Lunar storyline, and it just doesn't make any sense. Lunar Exalted were added late in the development process (they were originally intended to be a purely antagonist splat) and weaving them into the history of the game has always been an afterthought. The narrative focuses primarily on Solar/Sidereal/Dragonblooded interaction, and most of those interactions are fairly well thought out and flow from one event into the other.<br /> <br /> But Lunars? The Lunars have always just been kinda... mashed in. They're lazily described and poorly thought through. They were conceived from the 'top down', as opposed to 'bottom up'... and what I mean by that is that it was determined Lunar Exalted should be a playable splat, what that playable splat should more or less be, and then an explanation was thrown together post-hoc about how all that came to be.<br /> <br /> One of the most important things the game line could to to codify the perception of Lunars is examine these issues. They need a compelling, tragic history instead of just... random plot jumps, loosely held together with a shrug.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:53:16-07:00","id":982148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982142#post982142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because the Lunars were by and large loyal to the Solars. 1e also mentioned them as going and doing in the night what Solars couldn't bring themselves to do, so it doesn't sound like there was much in the way of smiles or sunshine there, especially if some Dragon-Blooded were labeled as disloyal and ended up being devoured. At that point, the assassinated/cannibalized group becomes a pack of martyrs, and their names become rallying cries. Sidereals just have to make sure that word gets out.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're getting pretty far into the 'Age of Nightmares' first age interpretation here, which isn't really canonical outside of in-character dragonblooded propaganda from the castebooks.<br /> <br /> The portrayed First Age was actually pretty swell. The reason for the Usurpation wasn't ever-present dystopia, it was a shocking Great Prophesy that it was an act of massive hubris to believe in because things were seemingly going great outside of a few weird 'huh' moments.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982142#post982142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More faces that change at a moment's notice and which might very well become utterly horrifying. Besides, what if the family of the Dragon-Blooded had a member that ended up being eaten? Again, spending more time around Lunars might not translate to thinking more fondly of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure most Lunar Exalted were judged as individuals rather than a splat in the first age, and again, the vast majority of First Age Lunars that have been described to us were (at the time of the First Age) not overly monstrous or unsympathetic creatures when compared against other Exalted. I don't really see any particular reason the Lunar group would have been reviled. These, again, are prenaturally charismatic and good-looking people who have centuries to master diplomacy, message control and public relations in a quasi-modern setting. I doubt face eating was a real issue back in the day.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:12:47-07:00","id":982161,"title":"","content":"The Evocation model of 3e artifacts means we're much more likely to see equipment that's consistently remained in Lunar hands.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>success is the ability to go from one failure to the next without any loss of enthusiasm","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1115-the-hug-ninja","name":"The Hug Ninja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1115_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"324"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:20:55-07:00","id":982166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982142#post982142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, if they had them. (They didn't.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I may be misinterpreting... Are you saying that you think Lunars owned zero artifact weapons, armor, warstriders, or warships in the First Age?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T09:23:03-07:00","id":982167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982148#post982148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We're getting pretty far into the 'Age of Nightmares' first age interpretation here, which isn't really canonical outside of in-character dragonblooded propaganda from the castebooks.<br /> <br /> The portrayed First Age was actually pretty swell. The reason for the Usurpation wasn't ever-present dystopia, it was a shocking Great Prophesy that it was an act of massive hubris to believe in because things were seemingly going great outside of a few weird 'huh' moments.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'm sure most Lunar Exalted were judged as individuals rather than a splat in the first age, and again, the vast majority of First Age Lunars that have been described to us were (at the time of the First Age) not overly monstrous or unsympathetic creatures when compared against other Exalted. I don't really see any particular reason the Lunar group would have been reviled. These, again, are prenaturally charismatic and good-looking people who have centuries to master diplomacy, message control and public relations in a quasi-modern setting. I doubt face eating was a real issue back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is risk in relying too much on the 2ed First Age stuff as arguably it made any pro-usurpation force seem flat out insane or at least really short-sighted. <br /> <br /> But your point can be countered by another flaw in how Lunars are presented, their curse is never really that predominant. Even the craziest elders have fairly valid reasons for anyone to be insane whereas Solars and Sidereals cant navigate two steps without the curse curb-stomping them. The Solars of the First Age were portrayed by and large as mad ancients with the younger Celestials unwilling or/and unable to challenge them. The Sidereals just happened to have a far more insidious curse which combined with their extremely hierarchical nature made it difficult to impossible to question their elders.<br /> <br /> Lunars? I have yet to see one that has the inexplicable madness of the curse in effect (Raksi was driven mad by the Wyld, same with Ma-ha-Suchi, Ingosh &amp; Lillith were horribly abused, etc.) and they have two strangely sane elders (Deathflyer and Python).<br /> <br /> The Lunars were already scary and intimidating by nature, being Celestial gave them enviable position and if their curse was actually played up then it would be easy to see why the DBs would turn on them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:39:00-07:00","id":982197,"title":"","content":"Isn't Leviathan batshit insane for no good reason?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:42:57-07:00","id":982200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982197#post982197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't Leviathan batshit insane for no good reason?</div> </div> </div> </div>He was more or less driven insane by having betrayed his Solar mentor to save his beloved (which he failed to do) who was also his mentor's wife, so he is basically taking his rage out on the his subjects. But he is a better example of a 'cursed-crazy' ancient.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:47:27-07:00","id":982203,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't buy that as a reason to be as delusional as he is. Bitter, cynical, filled with rage, racist, paranoid, sure. But Leviathan looks crazier than that to me.<br /> <br /> And remember, he and Raksi were young at the time of the Usurpation. They weren't old enough to be Cursed-crazy when shit went down. I imagine it took time for Leviathan to lose his marbles.<br /> <br /> It's true that there don't seem to be a lot of examples of elder Lunars living back then being crazy independently of the Solars. But weren't there Lunars involved in Operation Wyldhand?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T10:54:55-07:00","id":982208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982203#post982203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I don't buy that as a reason to be as delusional as he is. Bitter, cynical, filled with rage, racist, paranoid, sure. But Leviathan's seems crazier than that to me.<br /> <br /> And remember, he and Raksi were young at the time of the Usurpation. They weren't old enough to be cursed-crazy when shit went down.<br /> <br /> It's true that there don't seem to be a lot of examples of elder Lunars living back then being crazy independently of the Solars. But weren't there Lunars involved in Operation Wyldhand?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair he didn't claim Luthe and embark on the crazy train until the Contagion some eight centuries later or so.<br /> <br /> I believe some were probably in Wyldhand but none were mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:22:50-07:00","id":982505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982166#post982166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may be misinterpreting... Are you saying that you think Lunars owned zero artifact weapons, armor, warstriders, or warships in the First Age?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, but by the time anyone could probably get to them during the Usurpation, they were probably gone. The Sidereals would probably have directed their theft or destruction, because why wouldn't you if you knew that your enemies were going to go get them? In turn, the Lunars are continuing to do this to the Terrestrials and Sidereals, because they operate better when no one has that kind of advantage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">We're getting pretty far into the 'Age of Nightmares' first age interpretation here, which isn't really canonical outside of in-character dragonblooded propaganda from the castebooks.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The portrayed First Age was actually pretty swell. The reason for the Usurpation wasn't ever-present dystopia, it was a shocking Great Prophesy that it was an act of massive hubris to believe in because things were seemingly going great outside of a few weird 'huh' moments.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> Not really, because, again, it only takes one incident, and if you have five millennia, it's probably going to happen at least once. Then the Sidereals make sure everyone remembers.<br /> <br /> I should note, I'm not actually buying that Lunars had more contact with Dragon-Blooded than the Solars or Sidereals did. Especially since Lunars aren't bigtime, massive-scale labor motivators, advisers who treat future events like architecture, or other, like archetypes. They can definitely win others over with heart to hearts, and other direct interaction, but they aren't civil organizers, they're warriors, tricksters, and shamans.<br /> <br /> </span></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm sure most Lunar Exalted were judged as individuals rather than a splat in the first age, and again, the vast majority of First Age Lunars that have been described to us were (at the time of the First Age) not overly monstrous or unsympathetic creatures when compared against other Exalted. I don't really see any particular reason the Lunar group would have been reviled. These, again, are prenaturally charismatic and good-looking people who have centuries to master diplomacy, message control and public relations in a quasi-modern setting. I doubt face eating was a real issue back in the day.</span></span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> They've always been werewolves. When the world is in chaos and the Exalted were fighting the enemies of the gods, werewolves. When the world is an idyllic paradise, werewolves. It's the inspiration for their existence.<br /> <br /> Granted, the reason for getting rid of them was probably way more politics, but it doesn't really matter how the Sidereals or whoever managed to do it, it was done, and the Lunars were driven out. Future books probably won't put too many details on this, because the concentration of the edition is on the present, not the First Age.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:33:52-07:00","id":982509,"title":"","content":"Wyldhand was billed as a military training excercise. There were certainly Lunars involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T19:43:23-07:00","id":982516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982509#post982509\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wyldhand was billed as a military training excercise. There were certainly Lunars involved.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also kind of irrelevant for the future, because it's from DotFA, and that's not really being used as the vision of the First Age, according to developer comments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T22:32:25-07:00","id":982555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982167#post982167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is risk in relying too much on the 2ed First Age stuff as arguably it made any pro-usurpation force seem flat out insane or at least really short-sighted.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think the First Age should be pretty great, just so the Sidereal Exalted actually RISK something and make an actual dramatic decision when they decide to do the unthinkable.<br /> <br /> The entire POINT of the Great Prophesy is it seemed, on the surface, like a pretty stupid idea when held in a greater context. What's the big deal about predicting an age of darkness when an age of darkness is already here? It becomes the Great Suggestion of Doing What We All Knew We Needed To Do Anyway.<br /> <br /> The High First Age had many glorious heroes, and many were prone to vice or (more often) uneven tempers that could draw nations into war. Even given this, the good these luminous beings did far outweighed the bad. More to the point, even if it didn't, the astounding manipulative power these people have... primarily Solar, but also Lunar... ensures the vast majority of people will love them. They aren't living in hiding like the modern age, remember, they are essentially celebrities.<br /> <br /> But that's good for the story actually. It makes the Great Prophesy a truly meaningful decision and sacrifice rather than just an acknowledgement of the current state of affairs. It makes it a prophesy rather than a status report. After all, it was a prediction of the future, not an appraisal of the present. It makes what the Sidereals saw actually horrifying rather than just 'duh'.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T22:51:35-07:00","id":982558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982505#post982505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, but by the time anyone could probably get to them during the Usurpation, they were probably gone. The Sidereals would probably have directed their theft or destruction, because why wouldn't you if you knew that your enemies were going to go get them? In turn, the Lunars are continuing to do this to the Terrestrials and Sidereals, because they operate better when no one has that kind of advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>But there's only so much sabotage and theft you can accomplish without forewarning your targets that something is up. The Usurpation only succeeded because the first and biggest attack came as a total surprise.<br /> <br /> In the reverse, stealing and sabotaging artifacts is also tough when your targets live in Heaven and keep all their cool stuff there.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this never happened, but it isn't enough to account for Lunars owning nothing from the First Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:17:21-07:00","id":982567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982558#post982558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But there's only so much sabotage and theft you can accomplish without forewarning your targets that something is up. The Usurpation only succeeded because the first and biggest attack came as a total surprise.<br /> <br /> In the reverse, stealing and sabotaging artifacts is also tough when your targets live in Heaven and keep all their cool stuff there.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying this never happened, but it isn't enough to account for Lunars owning nothing from the First Age.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> First I'm not a fan of magitech so please take this post with that in mind:<br /> I think that while looking at the artifacts and &quot;cool Stuff&quot; that may remain in the hands of the Lunars we also need to examine what has happened. The Lunars were sandbagged by the Usurpation, plain and simple sure a few ships at sea probably escaped and if Luthe remains as written they have a mostly intact city. The problem becomes the Lunars know they don't have the infrastructure to build more &quot;FLYING CAPITOL BATTLESHIPS OF DOOM&quot; and the one that they do control needs repairs from the centuries that it has been used to insert choice of drama here. The Lunars are fighting a war where they do not have the option of making arsenals of 1st/Shogunate/ age weapons. The Siderals can sense that kind of activity fairly well and use the Wyld Hunt and Realm as the big bad hammer. Now where the Lunars do have options to make warstriders, flying pony bots of doom, or whatever certain Lunars will be working to recreate the artifacts that they remember. The artifacts that the Lunars do hold are probably used when needed, that Lookshy squadron of Warstriders is pushing deep into the jungles near Halta and needs to be stopped, out comes the husbanded moonsilver landmines that flow up the warstriders and eat the jade.<br /> I like the idea of more personal artifacts for everyone. I'd like to see Lunars have stealth artifacts, rings that hide the tell with the ring taking the place of the tell. Direlances that when plunged into the heart of a beast drain the creatures lifeforce and allow a one time transformation into that beast (or person). And since warstriders are still a thing I'm certain that somewhere hidden by Workings there is an intact shock force just waiting for the signal that the Blessed Isle is now cut off no ships can leave so E-Day is here time to deploy and retake creation for the Glory of Luna or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T23:46:42-07:00","id":982580,"title":"","content":"And truth be told, it's not like the other exalts are in a <b>much</b> better situation than the Lunars overall - there was much both Sidereals and Terrestrials had to sacrifice and spend through the ages, both groups certainly suffered losses in the passing of eras and is not like they have access to the kind of resources to easily recoup them, quite the opposite of it in fact. All of that without going into the matter of internecine factional strife or how overburdened each group can be by their respectives roles as &quot;keepers of the world&quot; so to speak, among other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-08-2018, 08:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:03:36-07:00","id":982647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982580#post982580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And truth be told, it's not like the other exalts are in a <b>much</b> better situation than the Lunars overall - there was much both Sidereals and Terrestrials had to sacrifice and spend through the ages, both groups certainly suffered losses in the passing of eras and not like they have access to the kind of resources to easily recoup them, quite the opposite of it in fact. All of that without going into the matter of internecine factional strife or how overburdened each group can be by their respectives roles as &amp;quot;keepers of the world&amp;quot; so to speak, among other stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a good point. Exalted is a <i>post-apocalyptic setting</i>. Sidereals and DBs just did a somewhat better job of consolidating control over what survived.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about problematic Artifact access, I think Abyssals and their sugar-daddy Deathlords, and to a lesser extent Lookshy's sorcerer-technician academy, are where you should actually point. Thoses are the only places I can think of, outside Autochtonia which gets a pass, where anybody has really been cranking out artifacts factory-style.<br /> <br /> I'm really interested to see how those get reinterpreted in the new edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:11:52-07:00","id":982650,"title":"","content":"Well, for one, we know Lookshy has no such factories anymore. Instead it's described that they just know ancient and impressive techniques for making weapons and armor, which suggests to me just that they've been making weapons but not that they're pumping them out like a factory. I suspect it means that the Dragon-Blooded craftsmen of 3rd Edition forge extremely well-made mundane weapons and armor, and that they likely have some cool and old artifact weapons passed down among the gentes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T06:57:27-07:00","id":982669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982647#post982647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a good point. Exalted is a <i>post-apocalyptic setting</i>. Sidereals and DBs just did a somewhat better job of consolidating control over what survived.<br /> <br /> If you want to talk about problematic Artifact access, I think Abyssals and their sugar-daddy Deathlords, and to a lesser extent Lookshy's sorcerer-technician academy, are where you should actually point. Thoses are the only places I can think of, outside Autochtonia which gets a pass, where anybody has really been cranking out artifacts factory-style.<br /> <br /> I'm really interested to see how those get reinterpreted in the new edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say even that much is quite debatable - even in 2e Lookshy is protrayed as being all too conscious of the fact their reserves are dwindling and the Academy something of a recent effort at forestalling that prospect - something of a gamble and one not everybody amongst its leadership is exactly happy with. The factory-cathedral that does get mentioned is damaged, its broken resources and essence discharges used for more hands-on making of wonders - what is sort of like using a damaged but still kind working nuclear reactor's defective exhaust ports as a crucible or forge, if when one thinks a bit about it, might be said - not to mention that angle/image is driven home further by the simple fact whole place might be just one (not) sacrificed sun-child/solar away of breaking down and blowing up, taking at least a good chunk of the city in the process. So, very far from ideal indeed.<br /> <br /> And while the Deathlords might certainly provide their abyssals with respectable resources, there's the fact Deathkniughts are among the less numerous of the exalted, with the possible exception of Infernals or Exigents (depending on how one does or does not count them). Ferrari has a factory, but that does not mean their cars are plentiful, quick to do or affordable by any stretch of the imagination, so to speak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 05-08-2018, 08:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T07:52:54-07:00","id":982693,"title":"","content":"Again, I'm not talking about Lunars making ancient artifact designs, I'm talking about them <i><b>owning</b></i> none at all.<br /> Lookshy and the Realm are both depicted as owning <i><b>huge</b></i> arsenals of powerful First Age artifacts, both warships and personal panoply, while the Lunars (depending on the book) either own absolutely zero, or own some but are never ever allowed to use them. That is, Lunars are in the exact same position as Solars, for no damn reason.<br /> <br /> I feel like people are talking past me, because the posts replying to me keep responding to a situation that... doesn't match what I've read or asked about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-07-2016, 02:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:44:16-07:00","id":982714,"title":"","content":"Where do you get the impression in 3e that they don't have artifacts?<br /> <br /> Of course they don't have a fuckhuge store of them like the Terrestrial Host does, there's less of them, they are not centralized and they are fairly individual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T08:47:33-07:00","id":982717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982693#post982693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm not talking about Lunars making ancient artifact designs, I'm talking about them <i><b>owning</b></i> none at all.<br /> Lookshy and the Realm are both depicted as owning <i><b>huge</b></i> arsenals of powerful First Age artifacts, both warships and personal panoply, while the Lunars (depending on the book) either own absolutely zero, or own some but are never ever allowed to use them. That is, Lunars are in the exact same position as Solars, for no damn reason.<br /> <br /> I feel like people are talking past me and not seeing what I type, because the posts I see keep replying to a situation that... has no resemblance to what I've seen and read or asked about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lookshy and the Realm had unified places to stash their stuff (and the size of their stashes is up for debate, since Lookshy is only a single city state and some redoubts, and anything they have has to fit in those limited spaces). The Lunars did not. The Lunars have been the #1 target of the world for thirteen to fifteen centuries. Whatever they brought along could not have lasted for very many years of that exile, so at present, they don't have massive, unified stores of First Age wonders.<br /> <br /> You don't get the benefits of squatting on the Solars' old empire if you're not squatting on the Solars' old empire. And once someone is squatting it, they can obliterate anyone who challenges them with relative ease until the lights go out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:07:32-07:00","id":982728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982693#post982693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, I'm not talking about Lunars making ancient artifact designs, I'm talking about them <i><b>owning</b></i> none at all.<br /> Lookshy and the Realm are both depicted as owning <i><b>huge</b></i> arsenals of powerful First Age artifacts, both warships and personal panoply, while the Lunars (depending on the book) either own absolutely zero, or own some but are never ever allowed to use them. That is, Lunars are in the exact same position as Solars, for no damn reason.<br /> <br /> I feel like people are talking past me and not seeing what I type, because the posts I see keep replying to a situation that... has no resemblance to what I've seen and read or asked about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that their gear being missing actually not logical (neither is their isolation from previous editions), they have been at this for millennia and their entire theme is malleability.<br /> <br /> I think that they should have hidden staches and ware-houses, there are numerous means to establish fortresses or reclaim them in the Wyld (Stability artifacts, Workings, Ancient Wyld-Forged outposts). It makes more sense that they would have good stuff and deploy it cautiously (with more viable causes warranting more of a commitment). That protects them from Sidereals (Cant see them) and DBs (kinda Wyld-phobic) and allows for drama when a major project like Halta is threatened and the Lunars begin deploying Artifacts en masse.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11320,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","user":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","date":". 10-06-2016, 12:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:24:57-07:00","id":982736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982728#post982728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is that their gear being missing actually not logical (neither is their isolation from previous editions), they have been at this for millennia and their entire theme is malleability.<br /> <br /> I think that they should have hidden staches and ware-houses, there are numerous means to establish fortresses or reclaim them in the Wyld (Stability artifacts, Workings, Ancient Wyld-Forged outposts). It makes more sense that they would have good stuff and deploy it cautiously (with more viable causes warranting more of a commitment). That protects them from Sidereals (Cant see them) and DBs (kinda Wyld-phobic) and allows for drama when a major project like Halta is threatened and the Lunars begin deploying Artifacts en masse.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to be surprised if Lunars were responsible for Halta in this edition, or care about it specifically. Or the Haslanti. Or the Delzahn. Or... well, you get the idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T09:38:08-07:00","id":982744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982736#post982736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm going to be surprised if Lunars were responsible for Halta in this edition, or care about it specifically. Or the Haslanti. Or the Delzahn. Or... well, you get the idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, still think it works as a general idea but YMMV.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:01:41-07:00","id":982761,"title":"","content":"I disagree; it probably won't be presented the same way, but taking Lunar-influenced societies and saying &quot;nope, Lunars didn't have anything to do with them&quot; is not a good way to make Lunars more involved in the setting.<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater appearing as a powerful barbarian god-hero-general, uniting the people against the Guild, and building a mighty federation seems entirely appropriate for Lunars in 3rd edition. Also, as the Haslanti have a barbarian aesthetic yet are in fact one of the most technologically advanced societies in Exalted, they fit nicely with Lunars without saying &quot;Lunars want everyone to be political barbarians burning down cities&quot; because in fact they're a democratic federation that totally loves using advanced tech if they can get it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:35:46-07:00","id":982776,"title":"","content":"Barbarian Punk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:43:36-07:00","id":982786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982761#post982761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree; it probably won't be presented the same way, but taking Lunar-influenced societies and saying &quot;nope, Lunars didn't have anything to do with them&quot; is not a good way to make Lunars more involved in the setting.<br /> Gerd Marrow-Eater appearing as a powerful barbarian god-hero-general, uniting the people against the Guild, and building a mighty federation seems entirely appropriate for Lunars in 3rd edition. Also, as the Haslanti have a barbarian aesthetic yet are in fact one of the most technologically advanced societies in Exalted, they fit nicely with Lunars without saying &quot;Lunars want everyone to be political barbarians burning down cities&quot; because in fact they're a democratic federation that totally loves using advanced tech if they can get it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's necessary to remove much of it because otherwise there would have been a much more enthusiastic response from the Realm that would have killed all of the Haslanti, albeit at a cost. Also, Scavenger Sons didn't need Lunars to make any of the locales it introduced. The only one that might have had Lunar backing, and very recently at that, was Farhold, and it was only obliquely hinted at until E:tL came out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T10:58:02-07:00","id":982796,"title":"","content":"The Realm couldn't mount a huge response because Haslanti is really, really far away, past swathes of territory they don't control.<br /> <br /> Would you prefer a setting where the Lunars secretly influence societies because they can't do it in public? That's what 2nd ed went for, and to many it felt like Lunars just weren't doing much.<br /> They need to be much more active this edition. And saying &quot;those things they did before, nope they didn't do them&quot; isn't a good way to make them more active (there might be one or two you want to take out for specific reasons, I could see a reason to take out Tammuz from Chiaroscoro for example, but generally). There should be more societies led or influenced by Lunars, and they should be more open about it, and the reason the Realm can't just conquer these places is because they will lose, because Lunars are badass, and also pick places that are awkward for the Realm to invade (as with some examples in the 3rd edition book).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:22:32-07:00","id":982811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982728#post982728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that they should have hidden staches and ware-houses, there are numerous means to establish fortresses or reclaim them in the Wyld (Stability artifacts, Workings, Ancient Wyld-Forged outposts). It makes more sense that they would have good stuff and deploy it cautiously (with more viable causes warranting more of a commitment). That protects them from Sidereals (Cant see them) and DBs (kinda Wyld-phobic) and allows for drama when a major project like Halta is threatened and the Lunars begin deploying Artifacts en masse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's think about this. I sincerely doubt that &quot;The Lunars&quot; have large stores of artifacts lying around. Raksi, Leviathan, Ma-Ha-Suchi, I bet they all have artifacts. Do they go around sharing them? Maybe. Probably on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> The Realm's Houses and Lookshy's gentes are collective bodies of Terrestrials, it's what allows them to have things &quot;in commons&quot; such that they have stockpiles of artifacts. They're also sitting on the artifacts of the Shogunate and the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact is not that kind of organization. It is not a top-down model like they are, they're individual, there's not that many of them. <br /> <br /> I don't really see why we assume they don't have artifacts, since it's even mentioned they kill people who have Moonsilver artifacts. It's just that they don't have them in commons, individuals would have them, and you'd have to treat with them the way you would with individuals to part with their incredibly rare, powerful artifacts which they or their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s may be using, or they might have emotional significance because their previous owner was a friend or an enemy, et al.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T11:55:57-07:00","id":982828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982811#post982811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's think about this. I sincerely doubt that &quot;The Lunars&quot; have large stores of artifacts lying around. Raksi, Leviathan, Ma-Ha-Suchi, I bet they all have artifacts. Do they go around sharing them? Maybe. Probably on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> The Realm's Houses and Lookshy's gentes are collective bodies of Terrestrials, it's what allows them to have things &quot;in commons&quot; such that they have stockpiles of artifacts. They're also sitting on the artifacts of the Shogunate and the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact is not that kind of organization. It is not a top-down model like they are, they're individual, there's not that many of them.<br /> <br /> I don't really see why we assume they don't have artifacts, since it's even mentioned they kill people who have Moonsilver artifacts. It's just that they don't have them in commons, individuals would have them, and you'd have to treat with them the way you would with individuals to part with their incredibly rare, powerful artifacts which they or their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s may be using, or they might have emotional significance because their previous owner was a friend or an enemy, et al.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is that the previous model for the pact does not really make sense for both what they want to achieve and what they have done in 3rd. The previous models have them being incredibly isolated with only loose contact among the elders and youths forming typically temporary packs, combine that model with them being openly at war with the Realm, DB numbers and the reduction of power-difference and the Lunars should barely be alive much less claiming as much land as they have. One or the other but if thing's stay as they were before it is less 'a bear fighting a wolf-pack' and more like 'a slightly bigger wolf leading a band of puppies against a hundred heavily-armed wolves with opposable thumbs.' It would frankly be better if they at the very least adopt a cell structure with a more thorough communication network.<br /> <br /> For the record I was referring to weapons that are not solely Evication-based (I'd be surprised if implosion bows are) which could be deployed to even the odds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:19:20-07:00","id":982846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982717#post982717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't get the benefits of squatting on the Solars' old empire if you're not squatting on the Solars' old empire. And once someone is squatting it, they can obliterate anyone who challenges them with relative ease until the lights go out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Though, technically, the people squatting on the most magically dense part of the Solars' empire are the Scavenger Lands, the heart of the Old Realm. (That's never been the Blessed Isle, in canon). <br /> <br /> (More broadly, it was quite widely distributed, and how much do the Realm control?)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982811#post982811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's think about this. I sincerely doubt that &quot;The Lunars&quot; have large stores of artifacts lying around. Raksi, Leviathan, Ma-Ha-Suchi, I bet they all have artifacts. Do they go around sharing them? Maybe. Probably on an individual basis.<br /> <br /> The Realm's Houses and Lookshy's gentes are collective bodies of Terrestrials, it's what allows them to have things &quot;in commons&quot; such that they have stockpiles of artifacts. They're also sitting on the artifacts of the Shogunate and the Old Realm.<br /> <br /> The Silver Pact is not that kind of organization. It is not a top-down model like they are, they're individual, there's not that many of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Think more, like, the Lunars have artefacts more like the Deathlords have artefacts than the Realm has artefacts? (Unless the Deathlord + Abyssal model is still too tightly bound for Lunars?).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T12:25:57-07:00","id":982851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982846#post982846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Think more, like, the Lunars have artefacts more like the Deathlords have artefacts than the Realm has artefacts? (Unless the Deathlord + Abyssal model is still too tightly bound for Lunars?).</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that the Deathlord Abyssal model has changed from Master/Servant to Master/Apprentice, it might be that they've both moved closer to one another!<br /> <br /> That said, I imagine that Lunar Elders, separate from this Abyssal comparison, might be categorically less interested in providing really good or really valuable resources like especially powerful artifacts to any theoretical lunar proteges they might have. I'm sure they've seen too many Lunars die over the centuries to get attached too easily, and might prefer holding onto their powerful goods for when said Lunars are more experienced or to trade them with another Lunar who is powerful enough to provide aid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:06:04-07:00","id":982917,"title":"","content":"I think they ought to have outright magical infrastructure centers, and I'll tell you why - if only to be critical of the 'rubbing rocks together and singing to trees' cliche again.<br /> <br /> We all have heard the line - 'The Lunar Exalted don't build up a city filled with artisans because the Wyld Hunt will come crush it!'<br /> <br /> Let's examine that.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt hasn't crushed Mahalanka. It hasn't crushed the Nameless Lair. It hasn't crushed Luthe. All of these locations are well known, even infamous.<br /> <br /> So let's point out something that's already implicit in the text - the Wyld Hunt cannot simply be everywhere. Many, many places in the world are simply too much of a pain in the ass to make it worthwhile to project force there. And it's ALWAYS been this way, because several of the aforementioned locations existed even during the heyday of the Wyld Hunt! So that justification for why Lunar Exalted don't create artifacts of that type doesn't really hold water.<br /> <br /> So we know that the Lunar Host in practical terms can, and does, secure territory and cities. Some were claimed post-usurpation and never unclaimed. And do you know what they do with them?<br /> <br /> Let them fall into ruin, of course!<br /> <br /> Every single one! Without fail!<br /> <br /> Because, of COURSE that's what people who were culturally part of the first age for thousands of years... brought up in a technomagical utopia, and trained and educated in all manner of sciences... would do! Throw on the animal skins, start a buncha fires, and break all the artifacts! HOWL AT THE MOON! Right?<br /> <br /> I propose that in fact, if enterprising Lunar Exalted were interested, it wouldn't be at all difficult to find a place in the MASSIVE LANDMASS of Creation to start an entire civilization dedicated to the construction of magical artifacts. It might not be oceanside Realm property, mind, but it would not have a problem existing. Wyld Hunt kill teams would not arrive. They're more concerned with the lower hanging fruit.<br /> <br /> And further, I propose that this probably should have happened already. Somewhere in Creation, a Lunar Lookshy might/should exist, waiting for you to write it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:15:12-07:00","id":982923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they ought to have outright magical infrastructure centers, and I'll tell you why - if only to be critical of the 'rubbing rocks together and singing to trees' cliche again.<br /> <br /> We all have heard the line - 'The Lunar Exalted don't build up a city filled with artisans because the Wyld Hunt will come crush it!'<br /> <br /> Let's examine that.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt hasn't crushed Mahalanka. It hasn't crushed the Nameless Lair. It hasn't crushed Luthe. All of these locations are well known, even infamous.<br /> <br /> So let's point out something that's already implicit in the text - the Wyld Hunt cannot simply be everywhere. Many, many places in the world are simply too much of a pain in the ass to make it worthwhile to project force there. And it's ALWAYS been this way, because several of the aforementioned locations existed even during the heyday of the Wyld Hunt! So that justification for why Lunar Exalted don't create artifacts of that type doesn't really hold water.<br /> <br /> So we know that the Lunar Host in practical terms can, and does, secure territory and cities. Some were claimed post-usurpation and never unclaimed. And do you know what they do with them?<br /> <br /> Let them fall into ruin, of course!<br /> <br /> Every single one! Without fail!<br /> <br /> Because, of COURSE that's what people who were culturally part of the first age for thousands of years... brought up in a technomagical utopia, and trained and educated in all manner of sciences... would do! Throw on the animal skins, start a buncha fires, and break all the artifacts! HOWL AT THE MOON! Right?<br /> <br /> I propose that in fact, if enterprising Lunar Exalted were interested, it wouldn't be at all difficult to find a place in the MASSIVE LANDMASS of Creation to start an entire civilization dedicated to the construction of magical artifacts. It might not be oceanside Realm property, mind, but it would not have a problem existing. Wyld Hunt kill teams would not arrive. They're more concerned with the lower hanging fruit.<br /> <br /> And further, I propose that this probably should have happened already. Somewhere in Creation, a Lunar Lookshy might/should exist, waiting for you to write it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I could not agree with you more! <br /> <br /> I would also like to see Lunars actually making things and not being severely outstripped by even mortals as artisans. <br /> <br /> I personally blame peoples fascination with keeping Creation on a permanent downward spiral and 2ed for aggravating that preference by going too far in the other direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:32:03-07:00","id":982934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982923#post982923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I could not agree with you more!<br /> <br /> I would also like to see Lunars actually making things and not being severely outstripped by even mortals as artisans.<br /> <br /> I personally blame peoples fascination with keeping Creation on a permanent downward spiral and 2ed for aggravating that preference by going too far in the other direction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I really prefer that Creation's downward spiral owe more to <i>fifteen centuries of nonstop war </i>with a total collapse of institutional trust and cooperation between anyone than to the disappearance of the Solars. The latter certainly didn't <i>help</i>, but making it <i>all</i> about the loss of Solar genius and artifice feels more than slightly masturbatory, and has a bad tendency to lend itself to the prevailing attitude of &quot;Let's rebuild the First Age, which was the objective high water mark for all civilization ever, exactly as it was; this time it TOTALLY won't end in madness and horror, we swear&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:33:12-07:00","id":982935,"title":"","content":"Those places where Lunars do build up a base they can protect may go in more for sorcerous workings over the landscape, and geomancy, and bound and created spirits, than anything that looks much like machinery.<br /> <br /> And this is one of those things where we all have variance on how much of that stuff we would prefer was about relative to machinery in the First Age, (also however much there was, my impression of Lunars would tend to be less tool and machine based than Solars).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T14:33:49-07:00","id":982936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think they ought to have outright magical infrastructure centers, and I'll tell you why - if only to be critical of the 'rubbing rocks together and singing to trees' cliche again.<br /> <br /> We all have heard the line - 'The Lunar Exalted don't build up a city filled with artisans because the Wyld Hunt will come crush it!'<br /> <br /> Let's examine that.<br /> <br /> The Wyld Hunt hasn't crushed Mahalanka. It hasn't crushed the Nameless Lair. It hasn't crushed Luthe. All of these locations are well known, even infamous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Luthe infamous? I thought it wasn't well known. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So let's point out something that's already implicit in the text - the Wyld Hunt cannot simply be everywhere. Many, many places in the world are simply too much of a pain in the ass to make it worthwhile to project force there. And it's ALWAYS been this way, because several of the aforementioned locations existed even during the heyday of the Wyld Hunt! So that justification for why Lunar Exalted don't create artifacts of that type doesn't really hold water.<br /> <br /> So we know that the Lunar Host in practical terms can, and does, secure territory and cities. Some were claimed post-usurpation and never unclaimed. And do you know what they do with them?<br /> <br /> Let them fall into ruin, of course!<br /> <br /> Every single one! Without fail!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, makes sense. Lunars who are socially minded probably have founded societies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because, of COURSE that's what people who were culturally part of the first age for thousands of years... brought up in a <b>technomagical utopia, and trained and educated in all manner of sciences... would do! </b>Throw on the animal skins, start a buncha fires, and break all the artifacts! HOWL AT THE MOON! Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>bolding mine.<br /> I really like the end of the first age to be a network of borderline nightmarish kingdoms. I say that at first to make it clear that I really don't like the First Age as utopic, and that informs alot of my thought process. That reasonging however is for another day. <br /> But even that aside....I don't think it was a) technomagical (anymore than mythic primeval ages ever are) in the sense that any of it was replicatable, or that the philosphies and ideologies of first age nations were inapplicable to guriella warfare, less advanced societies, and being terrible skinwalking nightmares. b) that lunars or any exalted from that time were 'scientific' or trained in sciences that would lead to more 'advanced' socieites when thrusted into leadership and retreating roles. The c) point would be that no-one said Lunars broke artifacts and chose to live on the priephary. They were forced to. Lunars probably have ancient artifacts, and I would give as much artifact access as lunars (the older stuff is in the hands of an elite group of elders who have no reason to let you have it, depending on the silver pact. But we'll get to that in your next point). But probably, said artifacts were lost because the Wyld hunt killed their owners and took their stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I propose that in fact, if enterprising Lunar Exalted were interested, it wouldn't be at all difficult to find a place in the MASSIVE LANDMASS of Creation to start an entire civilization dedicated to the construction of magical artifacts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree that artifact construction should be on any scale bigger than individual. This is part of why DBs might have more artifacts: They have (raw numbers wise) more Exalted craftsmen who might be of lower quality (might). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982917#post982917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might not be oceanside Realm property, mind, but it would not have a problem existing. Wyld Hunt kill teams would not arrive. They're more concerned with the lower hanging fruit.<br /> <br /> And further, I propose that this probably should have happened already. Somewhere in Creation, a Lunar Lookshy might/should exist, waiting for you to write it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The 3e Silver Pact seems to WANT Realm side property. The societies described are there to damage and sabotage the realm, and maybe eventually replace it. It's why the Caul (which sounds like the Lunar Lookshy you're describing) is so weird. It's where the Lunars have stopped fighting a massive guriella war and set up a functional base of operations. <br /> So there COULD be a Lunar run civilization. There might even be! I don't know! But certainly, the Lunar's agenda (as a group), lends itself to moving from revolution to revolution, warzone to warzone, and dealing with things on the move. <br /> <br /> That means Lunar infastructure is communication networks. Spy rings. Cults. Maybe safehouses, depending on the level of centralization. I expect they've done some crafting since then and some ancient artifacts are still in Lunar hands. BUT! When comparing to DBs (who out number them, semi-regularly hunt and kill the ones they find, and have laid down deeper roots) and Sids(who can have access to the later, along with an almost inassiable stronghold to retreat too), it's somewhat strange to say they should have more than or equal to the number.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:14:04-07:00","id":983020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982714#post982714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where do you get the impression in 3e that they don't have artifacts?</div> </div> </div> </div>We are talking past each other. I specifically said artifact-heavy sources which are <b>not</b> corebooks. That means no 3E books. Mostly only <a href=\"http://www.geocities.ws/the_incunabulum/exalted/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Main_Page\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. I also said that these sources constantly say that this or that First Age artifact is owned only by the Realm and Lookshy and Sidereals. I read the 3E artifacts section and IIRC no artifact says that.<br /> <br /> I know almost nothing of 3E; I have not had time to read the whole huge new book yet. If 3E drastically changes the way Lunars are depicted, I would indeed welcome a summary of the changes. (not sarcasm)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982936#post982936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But probably, said artifacts were lost because the Wyld hunt killed their owners and took their stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple posters have repeated this, but we have several examples of Lunar elders who have not been killed. So it is not possible for <b>every</b> last artifact to have been taken away from them. (And if there were no surviving elders, I would be complaining more about Lunars being helpless and unable to defend themselves.)<br /> <br /> Maybe you're only arguing that they have fewer than the DBs, and I'm misinterpreting? They certainly should have fewer, but I object to them having <b>none</b> whatsoever.<br /> <br /> The separate question is, if Lunar elders do own First Age artifacts (which a poster said they do in 2E), why they never make these available and never even use them themselves. I think that given the high casualty rate for very young Lunars, that a starting character is not going to have access to any more than a Solar does -- which is to say they should be able to raid tombs and ruins, including the tombs of Lunar elders, or try to kill DBs and Sidereals and Solars and take their stuff.<br /> <br /> But I do have some problem with the more experienced non-elders being blocked from using ancient artifacts. The Silver Pact has an overall agenda, and Pact elders aren't going to finance your random personal crusade. But if you're working to further their agenda, and you've already proven that you can survive and either kick ass or escape when shit goes down, why would they not be willing to equip you for important occasions?<br /> <br /> Put another way, the Sidereals have an arsenal First Age artifacts, and they probably don't hand them out like candy on a whim. But when you have an important mission for the Bureau, they don't ask you to go out armed with a stick and dressed in streetclothes, on account of the risk that you might be eaten by a Lunar or killed by an Abyssal or Solar, because those missions are <i>important</i> and the Bureau knows that if you don't put forth some effort and take some risks, nothing gets accomplished.<br /> <br /> Lunars can't stroll around like they own the world, but I really would prefer a depiction of them fighting a 1500-year war of attrition and <i>making a big impact</i>. Maybe even winning, <b>slowly</b>. At least capable of standing against other Exalted and not automatically losing. Lunar elders should be able to look at experienced young Lunars and judge them able to take care of themselves and sometimes allow them to use an artifact that is needed for accomplishing something for the Silver Pact. Elders themselves should have and use <i><b>personal</b></i>-scale ancient artifacts like weapons and armor and fire pearls and inexhaustible poison vials, and at least a few of the bigger artifacts like field artillery and warstriders, and whatever fleet Luthe has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-07-2016, 01:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:38:30-07:00","id":983032,"title":"","content":"Oh, I meant it's not surprising there is a discrepancy between relative number of artifacts among DBs and Sids vs Lunars, not that there should be NO lunar artifacts. I appear to have missed the exact point there, apologies. I meant that presumably elders are the minority of Usurption era lunars (being among the living) so plenty Usurption era lunars died and had their artifacts taken. Not that all artifacts had been taken, nor that no ancient lunar artifacts existed, just likely the majority weren't in Lunar hands (or were recovered by lunars after said murder team.) when compared to the # of DB made artifacts still in DB hands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:54:23-07:00","id":983043,"title":"","content":"That makes more sense. I took your post too literally, sorry.<br /> <br /> Lunars definitely should have less, and there's a good argument for them having a strategy of deliberately sabotaging anything they can't defend. In particular, artifacts that require manse infrastructure to maintain are probably really thin in Lunar territory. (They might even sabotage manses, to deny the DBs and Sidereals the use of them.) Eventually they got their hands on places like Mahalanka, and hopefully there are more Lunar dominions in 3E, but there must have been a period of time when they had no land. That means the artifacts they could keep would be:<br /> <br /> 1. Portable, by hand or in whatever Elsewhere storage Lunars get. This probably can include warstriders, though.<br /> 2. No infrastructure maintenance required. Maybe rules out warstriders, I dunno.<br /> 3. When they run out of Elsewhere space/hands/whatever, the first artifacts to go are the ones least useful to waging guerrilla war of attrition against the empire stomping on the human face.<br /> 4. Mostly in the hands of elders, but I like the idea of Lunar tombs and raiding them. It's just that all those tombs that were in accessible locations were raided by Lunars centuries ago, so in the modern era the trope is still mostly a Solar thing. Until you conquer a new chunk of territory...*<br /> <br /> 1+2 rule out warships and airships, except the folding ships and anything that was at Luthe.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Switching to one thing I do know about 3E, kind of a tangent, but if the Lunars control the whole Caul except Faxai, why haven't they destroyed the Immaculate Dragon Temple pilgrimage destination yet? Is it actually legitimately sacred to Gaia and they don't want to offend Luna? Or is it located in Faxai?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-06-2016, 09:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T17:55:14-07:00","id":983044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982846#post982846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Though, technically, the people squatting on the most magically dense part of the Solars' empire are the Scavenger Lands, the heart of the Old Realm. (That's never been the Blessed Isle, in canon).</div> </div> </div> </div>The heartland where it got its food, with some prestigious cities. The actual center was still likely on the Blessed Isle.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (More broadly, it was quite widely distributed, and how much do the Realm control?) </div> </div> </div>At a guess based on the number of sorcerers each side fields, probably about as much in use overall, with less emphasis on the terrible one-use stuff like the music box that rips out souls and more on implosion bows and ships. The definitely have way more First Age sailing vessels than Lookshy does by a wide margin; Savage Seas gives the numbers as the Realm having over a hundred First Age warships in its navy and merchant fleets combined (93 light, 19 heavy), while Lookshy has but five, and only one of them is a heavy warship. The Realm might also have more in storage than Lookshy does, because it has more places to hide them, but it also has more divisive politics, so a good portion of that might be monopolized by different houses.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Think more, like, the Lunars have artefacts more like the Deathlords have artefacts than the Realm has artefacts? (Unless the Deathlord + Abyssal model is still too tightly bound for Lunars?). </div> </div> </div>It could be, but the troves of the Grey Tyrants might change in this edition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-06T18:32:58-07:00","id":983061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983020#post983020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We are talking past each other. I am discussing artifact-heavy sources I have read which, as I said already, do not include <b>any</b> corebooks. That means no 3E books. I also mentioned, in the OP, that these sources constantly say that each artifact is owned in large numbers by the Realm and Lookshy and Sidereals. I read the 3E artifacts section and not one artifact says that. I was not talking about 3E at all.<br /> <br /> I know almost nothing of 3E, I have not had time to read the huge new book yet. If 3E drastically changes the way Lunars are depicted, I would welcome a summary of the changes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, backing up a bit, it changes a lot about how the world is presented. Warstriders are very rare and amazingly special, since they have both some hellish frontloaded capabilities and powerful Evocations, or are at least planned to; they're explicitly called out as being Artifact N/A, one and all. Anything less than that and you're just using a piloted version of the automaton stat block with some extra bells and whistles; not nearly so impressive, that.<br /> <br /> Pertaining specifically to the Lunars, their typical move is to make a territory into a temporary war dominion, rather than to shape a society that they watch for generations. These will almost invariably fail over time, but some do stand up, like the spider king's mountain, Robin Hood hyena women, and the example Lunar pirate fleet. Also, for Ma-Ha-Suchi, toss everything from second edition out the window. Ditto for Raksi, presumably. The latter is still a planner in the Pact, but the former stays out of the fight unless it comes to him, preferring instead to secure and expand his personal domain. <br /> <br /> (Also, the Caul is indeed sacred to the Lunars as well as the Dragon-Blooded; Luna walked hand-in-hand there with Gaia, so they keep the destruction of landmarks down, if possible).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T01:17:14-07:00","id":983211,"title":"","content":"One of the problems with 2E was that it presented the gap between Solar ability/MA/magics and everyone else's as more important than 80% of Creation's people would actually think.<br /> <br /> That said, you guys have made excellent points about Lunar resources; I probably need to reread 2E with less of a jaded eye. TY.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/476-argonometra","name":"Argonometra","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"534"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T05:29:30-07:00","id":983262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983044#post983044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The heartland where it got its food, with some prestigious cities. The actual center was still likely on the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm. I don't know. First book for Exalted - &quot;The Scavenger Lands were once the heartland of the Old Realm and have large caches of First Age magic&quot;, &quot;Scavenger Lands - At the heart of the Near East is the River Province, the military and administrative centre for the eastern sections of the Old Realm&quot;. Still, this is less decisive on the Scavenger Lands as the centre, to the extent there is one, of remaining First Age magic than I'd thought.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983044#post983044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At a guess based on the number of sorcerers each side fields, probably about as much in use overall, with less emphasis on the terrible one-use stuff like the music box that rips out souls and more on implosion bows and ships.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd think there's quite a lot of First Age ruins and magic across the world for Lunars to access, is what I'm trying to say. I think the idea it can't be accessed because it was all centralised on the Blessed Isle in the First Age is not a goer. Nor that the primary strength of the Dragonblooded Realm is that it is based in region where the most magical gear was based (I think they aren't, necessarily).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Argonometra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983211#post983211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the problems with 2E was that it presented the gap between Solar ability/MA/magics and everyone else's as more important than 80% of Creation's people would actually think.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e, or emphasis by fans on what the Solars could do and other persons could not because otherwise their return &quot;wouldn't mean anything&quot;? Not that I totally disagree with those fans, but I feel like you couldn't have envisioned something even like Ysyr in their view of what Second Age Creation (without Solars) should've been like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T08:26:15-07:00","id":983336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983262#post983262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd think there's quite a lot of First Age ruins and magic across the world for Lunars to access, is what I'm trying to say. I think the idea it can't be accessed because it was all centralised on the Blessed Isle in the First Age is not a goer. Nor that the primary strength of the Dragonblooded Realm is that it is based in region where the most magical gear was based (I think they aren't, necessarily).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Dragon-Blooded still have way, way more of their own to send out to look. One Lunar can get to one cache, but the same is true of one Dragon-Blooded. Numbers are a pretty big advantage in a scavenger hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:03:36-07:00","id":983355,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hug Ninja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982161#post982161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Evocation model of 3e artifacts means we're much more likely to see equipment that's consistently remained in Lunar hands.</div> </div> </div> </div> Also some of the named equipment we've already got. For example, according to Scroll of Exalts Kajeha Lef\u2019s Direlance Luna's Kiss is supposed to be a gift from the Incarnae themself.<br /> <br /> In 2e that's just flavour text for an otherwise &quot;normal&quot; Moonsilver Direlance because it doesn't have enough artifact dots invested in it to be something different but in 3e it'd be a very different story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T09:22:15-07:00","id":983361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983336#post983336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Dragon-Blooded still have way, way more of their own to send out to look. One Lunar can get to one cache, but the same is true of one Dragon-Blooded. Numbers are a pretty big advantage in a scavenger hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>True. The Lunars might be a bit better at it though! (Per head). Not that the Dragonblooded of the Realm are poor, and I imagine Bronze Sidereals tend to arrange matters to help them out. <br /> (Really the balance of Dragonblooded numbers vs Lunars' abilities is whatever implies the two &quot;blocs&quot; have as many artefacts as we want each to have...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T11:50:02-07:00","id":983441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts#post981208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I read descriptions of Artifacts, those from the First Age are invariably either lost, or owned and made solely by the Sidereals, Realm, and Lookshy.<br /> <br /> I find this rather strange. The implication is that Lunars took no artifacts with them into exile, and remembered nothing about how to make them. The very few unique Luanar weapons that I know of were given away to a Raksha (Death at the Root) or abandoned (Islebreaker).<br /> <br /> This makes no sense to me at all. Lunars should absolutely have their own ancient artifacts and knowledge that is preserved nowhere else. They should of course have things they took with them and kept from the First Age. They were not universally murdered, nor were they stopped by American airport security on their way to the Wyld. They are the heirs of the First Age just as much as the Sidereals. There is a distinct imbalance in power, but the idea that the Lunars have retained nothing at all bothers me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Is there some book that I haven't read that details all the cool First Age artifacts the Lunars kept for themselves or still know how to make?</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course the Lunars took Artifacts with them into exile. They certainly didn't drop their personal panoplies on the battlefield or hand it over to the Usurpers. For me, this is just a function of the game books having limited space, and none of the lead devs have the time/inclination to count up references to make sure every angle of proper representation is covered. Individual writers are paid little, and are on deadlines. They write what they are inspired to write.<br /> <br /> Western culture is at a particularly sensitive time right now when it comes to things like diversity in media. That perspective has utility in the real world, but I don't feel it's helpful when analyzing the books. The books, even taken as a whole, are just a starting point, a small seed intended to birth nearly infinite stories. If something ought to exist, it's up to us as STs and players to write it. If the question is &quot;Why doesn't this exist?&quot; then the answer is &quot;Because I haven't written it, yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Particularly now that we have Ex3, I just read the book, draw my conclusions, and move on. The book is just a starting point. It can't account for even 1% of the tales of the Exalted alive in RY 768. By the time the entire Ex3 line is published, we still won't know the names of 1% of the Exalted, much less their histories and what their ancestors/previous incarnations stashed away for another day.<br /> <br /> In my Creation, Lunars have many secrets and treasures unknown to the Sidereals and the Realm. Unlike both, however, they generally don't have the infrastructure or organization to make more. Leviathan doesn't deploy his remaining First Age warships because he knows the Realm will make them a target, overwhelm them with sheer numbers, and he will lose. It's better strategy for him to prey on their shipping here, assist the Realm's enemies over there, and <i>wait</i>. He has time, after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:25:05-07:00","id":983451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983441#post983441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course the Lunars took Artifacts with them into exile. They certainly didn't drop their personal panoplies on the battlefield or hand it over to the Usurpers. For me, this is just a function of the game books having limited space, and none of the lead devs have the time/inclination to count up references to make sure every angle of proper representation is covered. Individual writers are paid little, and are on deadlines. They write what they are inspired to write.<br /> <br /> Western culture is at a particularly sensitive time right now when it comes to things like diversity in media. That perspective has utility in the real world, but I don't feel it's helpful when analyzing the books. The books, even taken as a whole, are just a starting point, a small seed intended to birth nearly infinite stories. If something ought to exist, it's up to us as STs and players to write it. If the question is &quot;Why doesn't this exist?&quot; then the answer is &quot;Because I haven't written it, yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> Particularly now that we have Ex3, I just read the book, draw my conclusions, and move on. The book is just a starting point. It can't account for even 1% of the tales of the Exalted alive in RY 768. By the time the entire Ex3 line is published, we still won't know the names of 1% of the Exalted, much less their histories and what their ancestors/previous incarnations stashed away for another day.<br /> <br /> In my Creation, Lunars have many secrets and treasures unknown to the Sidereals and the Realm. Unlike both, however, they generally don't have the infrastructure or organization to make more. Leviathan doesn't deploy his remaining First Age warships because he knows the Realm will make them a target, overwhelm them with sheer numbers, and he will lose. It's better strategy for him to prey on their shipping here, assist the Realm's enemies over there, and <i>wait</i>. He has time, after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the issue that many of us are pointing to is that previous works have <i>explicitly </i>pointed to almost all Lunars who have such arsenals doing nothing of worth with them. To use Leviathan as an example almost every time his arsenal is mentioned we are flat out informed that he does nothing with them. <br /> <br /> I don't mind them being vague moving forward (it might even be helpful at times) but it is unfair to say that this concern is unfounded when there is much evidence to the contrary in the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:50:46-07:00","id":983469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983451#post983451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue that many of us are pointing to is that previous works have <i>explicitly </i>pointed to almost all Lunars who have such arsenals doing nothing of worth with them. To use Leviathan as an example almost every time his arsenal is mentioned we are flat out informed that he does nothing with them.<br /> <br /> I don't mind them being vague moving forward (it might even be helpful at times) but it is unfair to say that this concern is unfounded when there is much evidence to the contrary in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Allow me to be more succinct:<br /> <br /> Nobody master-planned the number of references of each type of Exalt in the last edition. If you look hard enough, you are always going to find an angle from which the game doesn't mention enough of these Exalts doing this thing, or too much of that splat not doing the other thing. Rather than rehashing what amounts to the same complaint over and over (for a dead edition with a long-gone lead developer, no less), it's best to realize that the books CAN'T tell every story from every angle, open a text document, and start creating. Then post it here.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, you will find plenty of good examples.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T12:53:43-07:00","id":983473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983451#post983451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the issue that many of us are pointing to is that previous works have <i>explicitly </i>pointed to almost all Lunars who have such arsenals doing nothing of worth with them. To use Leviathan as an example almost every time his arsenal is mentioned we are flat out informed that he does nothing with them.<br /> <br /> I don't mind them being vague moving forward (it might even be helpful at times) but it is unfair to say that this concern is unfounded when there is much evidence to the contrary in the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>No one in the setting really does much with stockpiles of weapons unless they are attacked or they want to project force, and even then they're super-valuable resources so they tend to be used sparingly. Most of the firepower of the Realm is held in reserve as weapons-of-last-resort and/or deterrence, which I think describes the Lunar elders as well. Lookshy is the only group that I think is really portrayed as regularly totting out their warstriders, ashigaru and similar.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that we seem to be comparing the arsenals of the militaries of the largest power bloc in the world to the personal stockpiles of individual Exalted. Leviathan is powerful, sure, but he's not <i>the entire Realm Military</i>, or even the ruler of a similarly big wealthy empire. Thing about the sexy magitech artifacts like 'striders and airships is that they need big military-industrial operations to keep them running, because they're remnants of a time when that was the norm. Leviathan doesn't really have one of those.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:00:06-07:00","id":983478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blackwell</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983473#post983473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one in the setting really does much with stockpiles of weapons unless they are attacked or they want to project force, and even then they're super-valuable resources so they tend to be used sparingly. Most of the firepower of the Realm is held in reserve as weapons-of-last-resort and/or deterrence, which I think describes the Lunar elders as well. Lookshy is the only group that I think is really portrayed as regularly totting out their warstriders, ashigaru and similar.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that we seem to be comparing the arsenals of the militaries of the largest power bloc in the world to the personal stockpiles of individual Exalted. Leviathan is powerful, sure, but he's not <i>the entire Realm Military</i>, or even the ruler of a similarly big wealthy empire. Thing about the sexy magitech artifacts like 'striders and airships is that they need big military-industrial operations to keep them running, because they're remnants of a time when that was the norm. Leviathan doesn't really have one of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but to reference the western directional books he does not even bother with maintaining or even keeping track of his stuff, he specifically has several noble warstriders gathering dust in back of some random armories around the city. There is a severe difference in conserving power and letting your stuff fall apart because you can't be bothered with it. Also Lunars have never been portrayed as the use when needed sort. Raksi for example has her city because she wants the book and is only really interested in being the only one to have the city, she is never shown to really care about the city's other traits. Ma-Ha-Suchi is the only one described as even vaguely considering his arsenal as an actual asset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:04:38-07:00","id":983482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983469#post983469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Allow me to be more succinct:<br /> <br /> Nobody master-planned the number of references of each type of Exalt in the last edition. If you look hard enough, you are always going to find an angle from which the game doesn't mention enough of these Exalts doing this thing, or too much of that splat not doing the other thing. Rather than rehashing what amounts to the same complaint over and over (for a dead edition with a long-gone lead developer, no less), it's best to realize that the books CAN'T tell every story from every angle, open a text document, and start creating. Then post it here.<br /> <br /> Suddenly, you will find plenty of good examples.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically enough I actually did Homebrew a setting a while back that vaguely approached this angle except for the Elder being more or less comatose, should still be somewhere on the forums I think. But I do see your point, I like to think that the point of this thread is more to spit-ball what many of us consider a problem with past approaches to Lunars and a debate as to how to remedy it since Homebrew can rarely affect a core part of a Splat's ethos, namely that the Silver Pact seems a poor organization and the elders are more like exalted hoarders than mentors/leaders.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:09:49-07:00","id":983486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983441#post983441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Western culture is at a particularly sensitive time right now when it comes to things like diversity in media. That perspective has utility in the real world, but I don't feel it's helpful when analyzing the books. The books, even taken as a whole, are just a starting point, a small seed intended to birth nearly infinite stories. If something ought to exist, it's up to us as STs and players to write it. If the question is &quot;Why doesn't this exist?&quot; then the answer is &quot;Because I haven't written it, yet.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes it is, but Exalted fandom has been overanalyzing and drawing conclusions about what it means that this book specifically fails to talk about X waaay before that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Agree with the wider point - &quot;absence of evidence is not evidence of absence&quot;. Perhaps absence of inspiration. (Actually also what I was trying to say to Erin upthread in my first, but I think that failed to come across.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:14:00-07:00","id":983489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983486#post983486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes it is, but Exalted fandom has been overanalyzing and drawing conclusions about what it means that this book specifically fails to talk about X waaay before that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Agree with the wider point - &quot;absence of evidence is not evidence of absence&quot;. Perhaps absence of inspiration. (Actually also what I was trying to say to Erin upthread in my first, but I think that failed to come across.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted splat partisans: the OG SJWs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T13:57:24-07:00","id":983517,"title":"","content":"Do not crap my thread with your random and completely off-topic political crusade. This is a topic about Lunars, not real life. Lunars are 100% imagionary fictional nonexistant things, not a real life group. Nor are Lunars related, in any way direct or indirect, to any real life group living or dead. This thread has <b>no relation whatsoever</b> to whatever you're talking about. If you want to talk politics, this is <b>not</b> the thread for it.<br /> <br /> I don't give a shit about Lunar &quot;representation&quot; because they're completely imaginary. The concept is inapplicable to fictional groups. I am not a Lunar and neither is anyone else. Nor am I a Lunar &quot;partisan.&quot; Lunars are one of my least-favorite splats. IMO they're one-note Hollywood barbarians, weak as mortals, dumb as rocks, a badly-written flailing afterthought, and so utterly irrelevant to the setting that Exalted would actually make considerably more sense if they didn't exist at all. Despite being ostensibly based on Werewolf: the Apocalypse (a game I love) they are stupider, less tech-savvy, less magically capable, less competent, and less interesting than <i>any</i> splat in that game, <i>including some Rokea</i>.<br /> <br /> Disagree with me all you like, but do not threadcrap.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was hoping for constructive information and polite discussion, especially about what First Age artifacts people think Lunars <i><b>would</b></i> have if they were written well, or what First Age artifacts they have and use in 2E and/or 3E.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:19:57-07:00","id":983526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983517#post983517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do not crap my thread with your random and completely off-topic political crusade. This is a topic about Lunars, not real life. Lunars are 100% imagionary fictional nonexistant things, not a real life group. Nor are Lunars related, in any way direct or indirect, to any real life group living or dead. This thread has <b>no relation whatsoever</b> to whatever the Hell you're talking about. If you want to talk politics, do it elsewhere.<br /> <br /> I don't give a shit about Lunar &quot;representation&quot; because they're completely imaginary. I am not a Lunar and neither is anyone else. Nor am I a Lunar &quot;partisan.&quot; Lunars are one of my all-time least-favorite splats because they're boring one-note Hollywood barbarians, weaker than newborn kittens, dumber than rocks, badly-written as a flailing afterthought, and so utterly irrelevant to the setting that Exalted would actually make considerably more sense if they didn't exist at all. Despite being ostensibly based on Werewolf: the Apocalypse (a game I love) they are stupider, less tech-savvy, less magically capable, less competent, and far less interesting than <i>any</i> splat in that game, <i>including some Rokea</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I was hoping for constructive information and polite discussion, especially about what First Age artifacts people think Lunars <i><b>would</b></i> have if they were written well, or what First Age artifacts they have and use in 2E and/or 3E.</div> </div> </div> </div>My gut reaction says that they would have a great deal of exploratory artifacts. <br /> <br /> Long-Range communications, mapping artifacts, etc. Anything you would need to report in from the deep wyld. Aside from being governors and commanders Lunars are also singularly suited to be explorers so it would make sense that quite a few elders would have probably tried to dig out their survival gear before fleeing into the wyld, which would also be easier to escape with than dragging your warstrider or warship out of drydock with a rebelling crew.<br /> <br /> I am also inclined to think once again that they probably had a few outposts in the deep wyld at the height of the First Age that were well stocked. Those would have probably been raided and looted almost immediately since the usurpers would probably know about them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T14:55:49-07:00","id":983548,"title":"","content":"Good post. I think in a similar vein I could imagine Lunars having artefacts to summon transport (a moonsilver tipped wooden staff that you plant in a beach, then a ship rises up out of the sands, with the staff as its mast), survival (a wine-sack with an inexhaustible quantity of clean water, provided the ghoulish face on it is fed monthly on fresh animal blood), finding and bargaining with local spirits, knowing lore (a mask that gives you visions when you sleep that feed you with the language and history of a land).<br /> <br /> Really it's so broad, I find it hard to see what they would *not* have. But comms and remote sensing / mapping does seem like a particularly good example for rangers / explorers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:10:40-07:00","id":983556,"title":"","content":"Good ideas!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983061#post983061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, backing up a bit, it changes a lot about how the world is presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, somehow I didn't see this post before. Thanks for that info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> So there isn't new info on whether Lunars own any artifacts in 3E, but they are <i>doing</i> something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-07-2016, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T15:56:24-07:00","id":983575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983556#post983556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good ideas!<br /> <br /> Huh, somehow I didn't see this post before.<br /> <br /> So there isn't new info on whether Lunars own any artifacts in 3E, but they are <i>doing</i> something.</div> </div> </div> </div>The theme seems to be, &quot;artifacts are fewer and more unique in general&quot;, and there isn't nearly as much focus on artifacts <i>non-Lunars</i> own, either. An artifact is more of a special thing a particular person has, and collectively artifacts are much less a type of commodity governments stockpile for national defense. And finally, Exalted are being treated more as individuals and less as groups; I recall seeing fewer collective references to Exalt-types and more mentions of specific named heroes (who are also Exalts) doing specific things. (that might have been a personal bias in how I read the book, feel free to disagree!!)<br /> <br /> Taking all that together, I think we can infer something about Lunars and artifacts, which is that any given Lunar's access to artifacts, just like any other character, is primarily a function of that Lunar's personal circumstances, and only relates to them being a Lunar insofar as being a Lunar affects their personal circumstances. This Lunar at the edge of Creation is going to have a different story about where he got his daiklave than that Lookshayan Dragon-blooded, and yeah, maybe in some abstract way the latter is &quot;more likely&quot; to have one than the former, but Exalted are so rare and so idiosyncratic that talking about them in generalities misses the point. Each and every one of them is an outlier so no concept of central tendency is terribly useful when you're talking about a <i>specific</i> character.<br /> <br /> I think that's a really significant change over the way previous editions and writers approached both the Exalted and Artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T19:58:57-07:00","id":983705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983489#post983489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exalted splat partisans: the OG SJWs.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Since you seem to have missed the directive issued in other threads, don't throw around the term SJW as a pejorative. Don't threadcrap either, I've suspended people for it before and I'm sure it'll eventually happen again. Don't be that person.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T20:46:16-07:00","id":983731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gigaton-Falcon-Emu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983482#post983482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ironically enough I actually did Homebrew a setting a while back that vaguely approached this angle except for the Elder being more or less comatose</div> </div> </div> </div>Magnificent Jaguar actually was asleep, so maybe he has a slight excuse for accomplishing very little. (I actually don't know if he specifically has accomplished anything, but since he's a Lunar I can guess.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T21:50:12-07:00","id":983753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Totentanz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983489#post983489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exalted splat partisans: the OG SJWs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Guilty.<br /> <br /> But I like to think my efforts led to good results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-07T22:34:58-07:00","id":983762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983731#post983731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnificent Jaguar actually was asleep, so maybe he has a slight excuse for accomplishing very little. (I actually don't know if he specifically has accomplished anything, but since he's a Lunar I can guess.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, i do find it quite noteworthy that while being awakened only in relatively recent times, he already seems to possess a host/nation of followers of his own, going by the comics in 2e books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T19:58:27-07:00","id":984188,"title":"","content":"You know I always looked at it odd that Lunars had to be the loincloth barbarian types. Don't get me wrong I've played em that way. However I look at that big ol map of creation, throw a small pocket of wyld here.... apply a liberal dose of a being who has lived long enough to have a first age education there, less potent than solar but still incredibly knowledgeable craftsmanship here and just a touch of moving magnificent jaguar to head it up here and BAM Lunar Wakanda.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-08T22:34:33-07:00","id":984256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984188#post984188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I always looked at it odd that Lunars had to be the loincloth barbarian types. Don't get me wrong I've played em that way. However I look at that big ol map of creation, throw a small pocket of wyld here.... apply a liberal dose of a being who has lived long enough to have a first age education there, less potent than solar but still incredibly knowledgeable craftsmanship here and just a touch of moving magnificent jaguar to head it up here and BAM Lunar Wakanda.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, considering in its original context &quot;barbarian&quot; has more to do with cultural arrogance and mass slavery apologism - too things the Realm is infamous for, incidentally - and some of the &quot;barbarous&quot; societies contemporary to the greeks were as complex and rich, if not more so in the persians, egyptians or mesopotamian city-states cases, as the hellenic, i would say that is quite acceptable. Not to mention the Delzahn, Halta and the Haslanti also have lunar patrons and are far from backward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T08:34:17-07:00","id":984426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984188#post984188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know I always looked at it odd that Lunars had to be the loincloth barbarian types. Don't get me wrong I've played em that way. However I look at that big ol map of creation, throw a small pocket of wyld here.... apply a liberal dose of a being who has lived long enough to have a first age education there, less potent than solar but still incredibly knowledgeable craftsmanship here and just a touch of moving magnificent jaguar to head it up here and BAM Lunar Wakanda.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Wakanda typically has to be double-secret-hidden, else a Sworn Brotherhood happens upon it, rolls it for everything valuable, and returns to the Blessed Isle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T09:08:15-07:00","id":984450,"title":"","content":"That's why it has a Lunar (or two). Or a Lunar and his weather-exigent wife. To protect it from Sworn Brotherhoods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:10:01-07:00","id":984503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984450#post984450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's why it has a Lunar (or two). Or a Lunar and his weather-exigent wife. To protect it from Sworn Brotherhoods.</div> </div> </div> </div>Who outnumber them, and have access to the same kind of wonders in even greater supply. Basically, very few are going to be left standing, and they'll suffer horrible losses that will knock them down to typical Second Age standards of living and industry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T11:37:33-07:00","id":984526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=983753#post983753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Guilty.<br /> <br /> But I like to think my efforts led to good results.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say the core material in Ex3 was more thoughtful about providing play space for Lunar characters. Hopefully we will have an actual book before I'm too old to throw dice. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T12:54:56-07:00","id":984559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984188#post984188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">BAM Lunar Wakanda.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bI like how the movie Wakanda portrays it as kind of isolationist without acting as though its industrial base is some kind of big secret that can be kept in spite of things like the necessary logistics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T16:48:57-07:00","id":984652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984256#post984256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, considering in its original context &quot;barbarian&quot; has more to do with cultural arrogance and mass slavery apologism - too things the Realm is infamous for, incidentally - and some of the &quot;barbarous&quot; societies contemporary to the greeks were as complex and rich, if not more so in the persians, egyptians or mesopotamian city-states cases, as the hellenic, i would say that is quite acceptable. Not to mention the Delzahn, Halta and the Haslanti also have lunar patrons and are far from backward.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main thing to consider on this is in <a href=\"http://nobilis.me/quotes:on-lunar-barbarism\" target=\"_blank\">Holden's commentary on Lunar Barbarism</a>. The tl;dr:<br /> 1e went heavily for what he defines as 'ideological barbarism' in Lunars - the fantasy image of a barbarian as a violent and uncivilized person who prides himself on ithose qualities, going further than 'we live away from the dominant civilization and are sneered at by them', and all the way into &quot;civilization is soft and weak, we like wearing itchy dirty furs and wiping with poison ivy and wondering why our butts hurt, and then rolling a big city for riches before burning it to the ground and laughing all BARBARBARBARBAR&quot;.<br /> <br /> 2e shied away from that but had them only tangentially connected to what he defined as 'political barbarism'; they live and work with far-afield outlanders of tribes and cultures that are opposed to the dominant civilization not so much because they believe it to be superior [aside from trying to make it superior to overthrow the Realm, but this is because they want to overthrow the Dragon-Blooded, not because they have a philosophical objection to running water and advanced metallurgy] but because it's what they have available. But as a reaction to 1e's ideological barbarian being near-universally despised, they lost a lot of the stylistic barbarian.<br /> <br /> 3e is allegedly going for a combination of stylistic and political. They supposedly don't consider themselves in the context of 'person from tribe' for long, simply because Exaltation tends to make you get a bigger picture [if nothing else, you'll probably be 'biggest guy in entire region around tribe'], but dress according to the cultures they're working with, ICly because it makes it easier to accept them and not see them as an unwanted foreign influence, and OOCly because that was the aesthetic the developers wanted to go with for Lunars as a primary course. So the NPC Lunars we see will wear mongolian-styled furs or Apache style feathered war bonnets instead of silk kimono or Daogong-era cheongsam or whatnot, but they aren't all 'tear apart the interior plumbing barbarbar' like 1e. It's more 'kick out the Dragon-Blooded so we can get revenge and have the benefits of infrastructure'.<br /> <br /> This information is of course about two or three years old at this point, I think? But it's what we know so far at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 10-09-2016, 07:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:07:22-07:00","id":984658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984426#post984426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wakanda typically has to be double-secret-hidden, else a Sworn Brotherhood happens upon it, rolls it for everything valuable, and returns to the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence a pocket of wyld. Where fate can't spy, and terrestrials tend to not exactly have an easy time of scouring. Get a no moon and some acolytes to provide ritualized sorcerous workings to keep their territory stable.<br /> <br /> Actually in one game I hid it right where no one expected an ancient civilization to be. The Lair of Ma Ha Suchi. rewrote the canon that his entire civilization destroying rage was a facade strictly as a front to dissuade anyone from coming in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying lunars can't do that is a disservice to an entire splat. Its not their normal wheelhouse sure, but it isn't a terrestrials wheelhouse to successfully utilize an ancient supermanse and we saw how that turned out didn't we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1777-kell_tamer","name":"Kell_Tamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1777_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T17:27:06-07:00","id":984668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kell_Tamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984658#post984658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hence a pocket of wyld. Where fate can't spy, and terrestrials tend to not exactly have an easy time of scouring. Get a no moon and some acolytes to provide ritualized sorcerous workings to keep their territory stable.<br /> <br /> Actually in one game I hid it right where no one expected an ancient civilization to be. The Lair of Ma Ha Suchi. rewrote the canon that his entire civilization destroying rage was a facade strictly as a front to dissuade anyone from coming in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saying lunars can't do that is a disservice to an entire splat. Its not their normal wheelhouse sure, but it isn't a terrestrials wheelhouse to successfully utilize an ancient supermanse and we saw how that turned out didn't we?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wonderful, another Island Five. Great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T18:58:19-07:00","id":984709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984668#post984668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, wonderful, another Island Five. Great.</div> </div> </div> </div>Be fair, the problems with Island Five went <i>waaaaay </i>beyond dumb 2e metaphysics.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T20:56:43-07:00","id":984737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984668#post984668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, wonderful, another Island Five. Great.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider myself a stubborn advocate of 2ed on alot of things but even I cannot defend that clustercluck of derp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11320-gigaton-falcon-emu","name":"Gigaton-Falcon-Emu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"786"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T21:19:49-07:00","id":984745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984709#post984709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Be fair, the problems with Island Five went <i>waaaaay </i>beyond dumb 2e metaphysics.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then they copied it and called it The Rutting Pens. And while that, too, had problems stemming from other material, you can only have so many areas concealed by Wyld anomalies before it starts to wear thin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-09T22:40:57-07:00","id":984752,"title":"","content":"Generally speaking, the &quot;Lunars don't have many artifacts, and haven't been able to make artifacts much&quot; thing is an intentional aspect of the way the game is set up. Artifacts are supposed to be rare, and having the bulk of them is meant to be a defining feature of the DB place in the setting. Some Lunars still manage to craft things, yes, but inventing an elaborate explanation for how they could have crafted large numbers of artifacts is self-defeating - the things you're trying to explain away were <i>intentionally put there specifically to make it credible that Lunars have made few artifacts</i>.<br /> <br /> Nothing stops you from making a Lunar-made artifact and giving it a backstory about how they put it together; in fact, the difficulty the setting imposes on that sort of thing only makes the ones they do make more special. The Wyld Hunt isn't omnipresent, and Creation is huge; you don't really need a complicated explanation for how a Lunar slipped through the net long enough to build something cool. It's just something that is (or at least was) very difficult and dangerous for them.<br /> <br /> But &quot;oh Lunars can just poop out a special off-the-grid stabilized Wyld bubble whenever they want&quot; is missing the point. The setting heavily depends on the fact that DBs, Sidereals, and Lunars have not, generally speaking, been able to produce many world-shaking wonders over the past 1500 years. That cannot change without making the entire setting collapse.<br /> <br /> (On top of this, consider that &quot;structural&quot; explanations for why Sidereals and Lunars didn't - Sidereals haven't had the time, Lunars haven't had the resources and have been on the run - allow Sidereals and Lunars to have decent crafting charms with the setting explanation that they haven't been using them too much for the past 1500 years because of those things. If you remove that <i>setting</i> explanation, the only way to avoid a setting comically awash in world-shaking wonders is to nerf Sidereal and Lunar crafting into the ground. It's much better to say eg. &quot;yes, a Sidereal or Lunar can build those things if they have the time and resources, but up until now, they haven't been able to for various reasons that are, to some extent, less applicable now&quot; so PCs who play those splats can still dip their toes into bigger crafting projects if they want.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-10-2016, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T00:30:47-07:00","id":984774,"title":"","content":"Sorcerous workings systems seems quite good for setting the implied bounds to Craft that feel appropriate to each form of Exalted? Since they feel appropriate when I read the ambition descriptions as the bounds of Sorcery each Exalted can do without really, really, uncommon strenuous effort. When you read the Solar Workings, especially at higher ambition, those feel like things that a Lunar or Sidereal shouldn't be able to do in the canon setting, even as once in a lifetime events.<br /> <br /> Whether an artefact is &quot;world shaking&quot; doesn't seem like such a good way of setting bounds because it seems like it's saying &quot;If you can change your world, even locally, with this, then it's out of bounds&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T01:19:42-07:00","id":984784,"title":"","content":"Lunars actually <i>can</i> do the top-tier workings. It's not a rigid thing like that. (In fact, even DBs can do all but the very top-tier Ambition 3 Solar workings.)<br /> <br /> But &quot;once in a lifetime event&quot; sells it short. I think Hatewheel said something about the transition from 2e to 3e about how, in 2e, the game and the fanbase in particular mostly fixated on the Exalted version of Sephiroth - the most over-the-top ridiculously powerful optimal character who achieves everything in their specialty they could conceivably do, and many things outside it.<br /> <br /> Most Exalted are not like that. The hypothetical Exalt who has every charm in their area of expertise rarely exists. Most Exalted never do the absolute limit of what the rules allow them to do. The Exalted are masterful, but they are not <i>literally</i> perfect. They make mistakes. They have limitations. Sometimes they're the peerless conquering hero, and sometimes they're Achilles in his tent, or Odysseus fucking up by pointlessly offending the gods. Even most Dawns do not actually devote their entire lives to a perfect flawless training regimen - they have loves, they have other goals and responsibilities, and these things conflict and keep most Exalted from reaching their hypothetical potential. (In fact, I'd probably argue that <i>no</i> Exalt has yet reached their &quot;full potential&quot;, to the extent that that's a thing, though some have come closer than others.)<br /> <br /> The same applies to the Lunar Exalted. They <i>can</i> perform Solar-tier Ambition 3 workings, or make even the greatest N/A artifacts. Most of them have not. It isn't a once-in-a-lifetime thing, it's a it-may-have-happened-a-few-times-ever thing. I mean, Solar-tier Ambition 3 workings are of course unthinkably rare even for Solars; we know of maybe one that happened, <i>ever</i>. It's likely that the vast majority of Twilights in the First Age never even attempted one.<br /> <br /> But that gets into what I'm saying above, in that the game relies more on &quot;here are the practical reasons why this doesn't happen&quot; rather than &quot;it is flatly impossible to do this unless you have a Tier 3 Exaltation&quot; or something like that. I mean - the practical barriers are higher for Lunars than Solars; Lunars need more means to make up for their disadvantages in attempting Solar workings, and almost certainly have far worse crafting charms if they want to attempt N/A artifacts. But it's not <i>impossible</i>, and part of the reason the game can say that is because the setting is set up in a way that provides an explanation for why most Lunars haven't been able to reach that theoretical pinnacle, especially recently.<br /> <br /> Because if they <i>did</i> reach it, even once in a lifetime, the setting would look very different. (And it would also somewhat defeat the purpose of having such a pinnacle by making it seem boring and 'expected' of all Exalted. Again, even most Twilights probably never attempt the top tier of Sorcerous Workings. It's supposed to be a big deal.)<br /> <br /> (By &quot;world-shaking&quot;, though, I mean &quot;capable of shaking the entire world&quot;, ie. an N/A artifact of such power that it makes everyone everywhere sit up and take notice. Lunars <i>are</i> theoretically capable of making artifacts on that level, but it's very possible that none have been made by them in the past 1500 years, and at most it would be just a few, as needed for individual stories.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":517,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","user":"Aquillion","date":". 10-10-2016, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T11:10:11-07:00","id":984956,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't mean &quot;Once in a lifetime&quot; too literally. Though I think it's somewhere between &quot;One in lifetime for every No Moon&quot; and &quot;Only happened a few times&quot;. <br /> <br /> (Like, summoning and binding a Third Circle Demon is a Solar Working, right? Unless I'm wrong, which I could be. So were there only a few times Lunars or Sidereals ever did that in the First Age? What's our POV? It could go either way, depending on taste.). <br /> <br /> But I'm not so bothered by if they did any Solar Workings at all ever (frankly it could be never in life time, ever). I'm more interested that the system sets useful and evocative bounds to Celestial Circle Workings that make them feel like the Celestial Exalted characters, who will be using them frequently and competently, and probably never using Solar Workings could really achieve something in changing the world, that's appropriate to their level as Celestial Exalted, versus relying on a more subjective &quot;Anything world shaking is too much and anything that changes the world and matters is world shaking&quot; sort of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T14:34:12-07:00","id":985074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984426#post984426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wakanda typically has to be double-secret-hidden, else a Sworn Brotherhood happens upon it, rolls it for everything valuable, and returns to the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>So are we ignoring that there's an <i>entire frakking continent</i> in the West where the Realm only has one walled stronghold and have been kept out of the rest by the Lunar forces there?<br /> <br /> Because The Caul is a thing.<br /> <br /> Lunars holding their own territory against the Realm is a thing.<br /> <br /> Right there. Right in the Core.<br /> <br /> Like, the idea of a Lunar Wakanda is entirely viable. Just &quot;There's a few Manses here in this territory on The Caul squarely in the control of Lunars&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T15:44:05-07:00","id":985106,"title":"","content":"Didn't the corebook portray control of the Caul as having gone back and forth?<br /> <br /> \u200bEven then, I think there's a question of how resources devoted to building something special and new are taken away from resources to hem in the Realm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T16:58:58-07:00","id":985133,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>whimsicalpigeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=985106#post985106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the corebook portray control of the Caul as having gone back and forth?<br /> <br /> \u200bEven then, I think there's a question of how resources devoted to building something special and new are taken away from resources to hem in the Realm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not the WHOLE Caul. THe Caul, IIRC, is a warzone, but it's one where the Lunars have staked territory, and atm is dominated by Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T17:39:24-07:00","id":985153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=984426#post984426\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wakanda typically has to be double-secret-hidden, else a Sworn Brotherhood happens upon it, rolls it for everything valuable, and returns to the Blessed Isle.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the notion that a Sworn Brotherhood can simply roll an entire kingdom or civilization no questions asked (even without Lunars or artifact goodies entering the equation) is an incredibly strange notion that is not borne out in the DB stats we have so far, nor will it be when we get a DB book.<br /> <br /> And that the idea that you can't have little undiscovered Lunar kingdoms (maybe even with a higher standard of living than their surroundings, or with unique goodies that the ST wants to introduce) because Dragon-Bloods are 100% guaranteed to have found them and kicked them over is a strange (and insidiously reductive) idea that vastly underestimates the size of Creation, and overestimates the power of the Realm.<br /> <br /> There's a sort of literalism that renders Lookshy the only dragon-blooded state opposing the Realm, Ejava the only Scarlet Pretender opposing Mnemon, and now, the Caul the only place where Lunars can set up shop. (&quot;Well okay you can have your PC be a claimant for the throne, but <i>only</i> if you play Ejava&quot; rather than &quot;you can build your PC to be a claimant for the throne, Ejava might help you model what that might look like.&quot;) It denies the essential vitality of a world that is supposed to be vibrant with legends and heroes. It denies the <i>exploration</i> of a world that is, frankly, mostly blank space.<br /> <br /> Are there reasons why secret Lunar kingdoms aren't on every corner store? Sure. Are there reasons why every Lunar doesn't have a death ray? Sure. Might the Lunar kingdom be sort of doomed in the long run, or the death ray a target for the Dragon-Blooded? Sure. Do you need a reason to give a particular Lunar you encounter a hidden kingdom or a death ray? <i>Not at all.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2144,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","user":"Guancyto","date":". 10-10-2016, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto","name":"Guancyto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2144_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"699"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-10T18:56:56-07:00","id":985201,"title":"","content":"Looking at some other dev statements, it seems that the simplest reason there won't really be a Lunar Wakanda somewhere isolated from the Realm is because they're not very good at it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T16:13:33-07:00","id":985754,"title":"","content":"Aquillion you make some very good points about why it makes sense for Lunars to have fewer artifacts. I hadn't thought about the connection to the quality of Charms, but it makes sense.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2144-guancyto\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2144_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2144\" data-vbnamecard=\"2144\">Guancyto</a>, well-said. The NPCs and kingdoms in canon are there as examples, not the sum total of all that exist.<br /> <br /> I really liked Holden's post about barbarism, and it's a hopeful sign that 3E might finally do Lunars right. I also appreciated reading that in 3E, being killed by Lunars is one of the biggest causes of Sidereal death. It's a good sign that they won't be written as helpless losers. So, I hope there will also be mention of Lunars owning multiple artifacts, using them, and even making them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:09:06-07:00","id":987753,"title":"","content":"As a little aside, <b>what</b> ancient artifacts would you give Lunars - or any other group of exalts for that matter - as relics of past ages and legends?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:13:12-07:00","id":987757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987753#post987753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a little aside, <b>what</b> ancient artifacts would you give Lunars - or any other group of exalts for that matter - as relics of past ages and legends?</div> </div> </div> </div>As noted upthread, probably portable stuff. Weapons and armor are more likely than anything non-transportable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:28:49-07:00","id":987766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987757#post987757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As noted upthread, probably portable stuff. Weapons and armor are more likely than anything non-transportable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but i was asking something like a style, aesthetic or maybe some examples. What says an artifact is of a certain exalt's making, beside (possibly, debatably) the magic material used in its crafting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T08:33:45-07:00","id":987768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987766#post987766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but i was asking something like a style, aesthetic or maybe some examples. What says an artifact is of a certain exalt's making, beside (possibly, debatably) the magic material used in its crafting?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems a distant secondary concern to what they could pick up and keep on their persons (which was probably mostly moonsilver in construction). If you have to leave in a hurry, you don't really have much time or concern for deciding if something is &quot;really you&quot; or not, and in a year or so of constantly being on the run, &quot;portable and easily carried&quot; is going to become the primary identifier of your style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T09:22:24-07:00","id":987788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987766#post987766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What says an artifact is of a certain exalt's making</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThe examples in the corebook make it look like virtually nothing is different between them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:17:14-07:00","id":987878,"title":"","content":"Based in part on <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=982567#post982567\">one of Incbill's posts</a> here are three attempts (I have no crunch abilities, though) :<br /> <br /> <br /> Moonsilver Mine<br /> In its dormant state a Moonsilver Mine is a disc about a foot across and 1 inch thick, which can be concealed under a thin layer of dirt, grass, or leaves. When stepped upon it rapidly flows upwards, consuming mundane weapons and armor and pouring itself down throats into lungs. It also severely damages artifacts, which require repair before they can be used again. Moonsilver mines also must be reset with a repair roll before reuse.<br /> In the Second Age, the Lunars retain many of these mines, which they carefully deploy to defend their holdings.<br /> <br /> Ring of the Hidden Beast<br /> A moonsilver ring which resizes itself to fit the attuned user. It hides a Lunar\u2019s Tell from all observation, taking the place of the Tell as a white ring around whatever appendage it's attached to. It can fit on a finger, toe, wrist, ankle, tail, or neck. A Ring of the Hidden Beast can be implanted as a tattoo artifact, if desired.<br /> <br /> Moonlight-on-the-Water Amulet<br /> With this potent wonder, a Lunar gains a great measure of protection from astrology and the Loom of Fate. Using the principles first applied to the creation of complex power armor such as the Most Excellent Armor of the Elemental Dragons, two elder Lunar survivors of the First Age designed a much simpler artifact to fool the Sidereals. They completed their first Amulets during the first centuries of the Shogunate, and spread the methods of crafting more among the Lunar Host.<br /> The most common version of the Moonlight-on-the-Water Amulet blurs a Lunar's fate while they wear any shape that is not one of their true forms. Their activities are still visible to the Loom and astrology, but only indicate the presence of the animal, human, or other creature whose shape they stole. This requires a daily expenditure of [motes].<br /> Amulets worth +2 dots actually apply a continual astrology-fooling effect equal to that of Dragon Armor and even benefits non-Lunars, but very few elders remain who possess the skill to craft such a wonder.<br /> (From 1E Dragon Armor: \u201cThe armor can also protect against detection by divination and astronomy \u2014 add +2 difficulty to all attempts to locate or determine the fate of the wearer, his armor and anything it is touching. This is proof against Sidereal astronomy and the foresight of the little gods. (This ability costs 5 motes and one Willpower per day).\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T12:39:42-07:00","id":987896,"title":"","content":"The first of those is very sci-fi, and I think the second is redundant with how the corebook describes that Lunar thing as working.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:24:58-07:00","id":987907,"title":"","content":"An obvious thing for the Moonsilver Mine might be shapeshifting itself to be better concealed than an ordinary trap, and/or that the Lunar can find it with better intuition than they could an ordinary mine, through intuition. I think its a devilishly horrible trap though. It is kind of techy, but its easy enough to just not call it a mine.<br /> <br /> I do think the problem with it, if there is one, is more that Moonsilver is a treasured rare and precious substance of Luna. It's like if you had an Orichalcum Mine or a Starmetal Mine. Is that really something that makes sense as what you'd do with one of the Five Magical Materials? In the sense of a mine as something that you sort of scatter around a domain and then just abandon and forget about, less than something you've placed in quite a specific place for an ambush and reuse.<br /> <br /> I like the idea of a ring that harbors and contains the Lunars' bestial aspects. I think there could be more that could be done with that theme in addition to hiding the tell, if someone wanted to.<br /> <br /> Moonlight-on-the-Water Amulet is a cool idea. I think I'd find it more fun to encounter as a Sidereal PC as a challenge (where is that Sidereal?). It seems like it'd be very dependent for utility on how innocuous what the Lunar is doing is, how well matched their activity is to the shape, and how observant the person watching the Loom is. &quot;The presence of One Lucky Shepherdess in Mnemon's bathing chambers came as some surprise to Falling Leaf, of the Chosen of Endings. Not least because 1) her Fate had been never to leave Incas Prefecture and furthermore 2) because she was dead.&quot;. However, I imagine there is quite a bit of flex there in the lazy gods and overworked Sidereals and in doing rather sneaky stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:37:42-07:00","id":987916,"title":"","content":"Maybe mine isn't really a good word, then? I wrote it to be something they find again and reuse after a battle, since magical materials are precious. I like the idea that it helps camouflage itself -- do you think that would extend to coloration as well as shape, or would that go beyond the whole &quot;always looks obviously magical and silvery&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Maybe if it kills somebody, it wraps around their artifacts, anchors them to the ground, and hardens, so that only the mine's owner can get those artifacts out.<br /> <br /> Would it be less &quot;techy&quot; if it attacked people by seeping into their pores instead of suffocating them? Or beat them with tentacles?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T13:45:17-07:00","id":987919,"title":"","content":"Even if Lunars didn't manage to carry many artifacts with them in their flight from the Usurpation, or lost them to Wyld Hunts over the ages, I'd still like to see lots of examples of things they <i>did </i>have at some point, which are now stored in forbidden tombs or Dynastic collections or even Yu-Shan itself, because adventure hooks ahoy! &quot;You want the long-lost blade of your original incarnation, forged as a wedding gift from your Solar mate? This Imperial dickhead mounted it as a trophy over the taxidermied War Form of your previous life. Here's his estate. Have fun.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T15:40:29-07:00","id":987966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987919#post987919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if Lunars didn't manage to carry many artifacts with them in their flight from the Usurpation, or lost them to Wyld Hunts over the ages, I'd still like to see lots of examples of things they <i>did </i>have at some point, which are now stored in forbidden tombs or Dynastic collections or even Yu-Shan itself, because adventure hooks ahoy! &quot;You want the long-lost blade of your original incarnation, forged as a wedding gift from your Solar mate? This Imperial dickhead mounted it as a trophy over the taxidermied War Form of your previous life. Here's his estate. Have fun.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a cool idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:45:54-07:00","id":988102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts#post981208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there some book that I haven't read that details all the cool First Age artifacts the Lunars kept for themselves or still know how to make?</div> </div> </div> </div>This is where the customisability of the setting and sourcebooks comes into play: Look through O's Codex and WotLA. See something you like? There is *zero* in-setting reason why any of those items can't be part of the panoply of any Lunar N/PC you put in your games. You can even devise elaborate systems for them, like a Pack of young Lunars who know that their Windblades all belong to their Friendly Neighborhood Elder, and their continued usage of them is dependent on successfully pulling off missions he sends them on. But what happens if one of them is stolen by that pesky Deathknight they keep running into...?<br /> <br /> Why doesn't the game's setting portray Lunars this way? Probably because they just want to keep up the image of Barbarian Heroes, who don't usually carry much magical bling. But if you want to play Thundarr rather than Conan, then go for it! <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-15T20:48:51-07:00","id":988103,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=985074#post985074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So are we ignoring that there's an <i>entire frakking continent</i> in the West where the Realm only has one walled stronghold and have been kept out of the rest by the Lunar forces there?<br /> <br /> Because The Caul is a thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Speaking of, wasn't there something about a secondary Loom of Fate that the Lunars have there, that keeps Sidereals from seeing and interfering with their Fates? Do we know if that's something from the First Age or of Lunar design?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T00:22:20-07:00","id":988163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hand-of-Omega</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=988103#post988103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Speaking of, wasn't there something about a secondary Loom of Fate that the Lunars have there, that keeps Sidereals from seeing and interfering with their Fates? Do we know if that's something from the First Age or of Lunar design?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know if there's anything in the core itself, but I remember in the leadup one of the devs saying that the Lunars cut away part of the Loom to make the Caul free from Sidereal influence. Which I imagine would put it Post Usurpation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T08:50:00-07:00","id":988262,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=988163#post988163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know if there's anything in the core itself, but I remember in the leadup one of the devs saying that the Lunars cut away part of the Loom to make the Caul free from Sidereal influence. Which I imagine would put it Post Usurpation</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't recall that. Just that they, through a taxing feat, managed to remove the Caul from the Loom and have a different system set up to keep everything as it otherwise would be in Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T09:43:29-07:00","id":988285,"title":"","content":"Sounds like sorcerous working territory. How would you break that down, in mechanical terms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/681-hand-of-omega","name":"Hand-of-Omega","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar681_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2747"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T12:53:17-07:00","id":988347,"title":"","content":"It'd probably be an Adamant working of some kind. It would probably either make Sidereal powers harder to use, or block some entirely.<br /> <br /> Of course, we'll need to know how Astrology works to come up with exact mechanics","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:22:30-07:00","id":988394,"title":"","content":"That doesn't quite read right to me. We don't have Abyssals yet, either, but that hasn't stopped me having a Daybreak necrosurgeon in my Okeanos group.<br /> <br /> If an ST wants to suss out the effects of the Caul on astrology, he can do so without having to wait years for the Sidereal book, provided he's willing to suss out the effects of astrology.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T05:01:48-07:00","id":988793,"title":"","content":"Yeah, until mechanics are actually relevant - a PC is playing a Sidereal character who is attempting to utilize Astrology in the area of the Caul - it's pretty much narrative, so the ST can call it whatever, whether &quot;It's more trouble than it's worth to use&quot; all the way to &quot;Astrological tampering absolutely does not work here&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the unlikely event that a game running now survives all the way to Lunars and Sidereals being released such that the Caul's specific impact becomes both mechanically relevant and proven more or less significant than determined, you can simply say something happened. The Sidereals weaken the Caul in some way or the Lunars strengthened it, to make the post-Sidereals Caul difference from Pre-Sidereals Caul justified.<br /> <br /> On the subject of what it is I would personally hope it's a Lunar-worked Sorcerous Working, guessing around Solar Ambition 2 [&quot;Alter major metaphysical properties of a city-sized region&quot;, increasing the scale in exchange for reducing the scope, essentially], to create a sense that yes, they can and do do things, they don't just scavenge the ruins of the first age and stare dumbly at the works of the Solars unable to comprehend creating even a shadow of their glory.<br /> <br /> ...yeah, 2e was <i>bad</i> about that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":756,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","user":"Meianno Yuurei","date":". 10-17-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/756-meianno-yuurei","name":"Meianno Yuurei","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T21:54:53-07:00","id":989198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987916#post987916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe mine isn't really a good word, then? I wrote it to be something they find again and reuse after a battle, since magical materials are precious. I like the idea that it helps camouflage itself -- do you think that would extend to coloration as well as shape, or would that go beyond the whole &quot;always looks obviously magical and silvery&quot; thing?<br /> <br /> Maybe if it kills somebody, it wraps around their artifacts, anchors them to the ground, and hardens, so that only the mine's owner can get those artifacts out.<br /> <br /> Would it be less &quot;techy&quot; if it attacked people by seeping into their pores instead of suffocating them? Or beat them with tentacles?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I deliberately went &quot;techie&quot; with the idea of the mine. I haven't sat down and created the moonsilver mines, and if I did I would have variations that were camouflaged by blending into the soil. I would have anti-personal as well as Warstrider versions. The example I used was to counter Warstriders. I have no problem with tentacles ripping from the ground to squeeze hapless soldiers to death. I have no problem with the others having similar artifacts. I would probably not make them re-usable and rare which is why I would limit them to anti-Warstrider weapons. I would also have a version that changed the ground from solid to quicksilver sand sucking things below the earth only to become solid.<br /> <br /> The ring idea again was a spur of the moment idea; one that I may develop further in my own campaign as spotting the Tell is a major issue with the Lunars. And yes I could see higher levels having interaction with DBT or even evocations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T03:16:11-07:00","id":989273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=987919#post987919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if Lunars didn't manage to carry many artifacts with them in their flight from the Usurpation, or lost them to Wyld Hunts over the ages, I'd still like to see lots of examples of things they <i>did </i>have at some point, which are now stored in forbidden tombs or Dynastic collections or even Yu-Shan itself, because adventure hooks ahoy! &quot;You want the long-lost blade of your original incarnation, forged as a wedding gift from your Solar mate? This Imperial dickhead mounted it as a trophy over the taxidermied War Form of your previous life. Here's his estate. Have fun.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe off-topic, but the idea of an Imperial dickhead who collects taxidermied War Forms of Lunar Exalted is DEFINITELY something I am putting into the next game I run with a Necromancer PC.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, no, even better! This is the setting for my inevitable one-shot when What Fire Has Wrought comes out. Dynast Teens In Danger, in the now-haunted manor of someone's Great Uncle, when all of his trophies come to life to seek revenge on their hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2223,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","user":"Ketrus","date":". 10-18-2016, 06:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T07:17:33-07:00","id":989337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989273#post989273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe off-topic, but the idea of an Imperial dickhead who collects taxidermied War Forms of Lunar Exalted is DEFINITELY something I am putting into the next game I run with a Necromancer PC.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wait, no, even better! This is the setting for my inevitable one-shot when What Fire Has Wrought comes out. Dynast Teens In Danger, in the now-haunted manor of someone's Great Uncle, when all of his trophies come to life to seek revenge on their hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a note, Lunar Exalted ARE Celestial Exalted. So by the metaphysics implied by the setting, the guy who stuffs one and uses it as a display piece is... having a bad time.<br /> <br /> When you kill any Celestial, what you do is build them a nice, proper tomb, throw them a lavish funeral, and bury them will full honors. You do this because Celestial ghosts are known to be very, very uppity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3386-piff","name":"Piff","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3386_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"442"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T09:30:18-07:00","id":989391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989198#post989198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also have a version that changed the ground from solid to quicksilver sand sucking things below the earth only to become solid.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Artifacts:Quagmire_Perimeter_Mine\" target=\"_blank\">a canon trap similar to that</a>, in jade. Apparently runs on an Essence battery which seems weird to me, but I guess that saves on having to keep it attuned indefinitely. How did you envision your moonsilver traps being &quot;powered&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T11:24:32-07:00","id":989453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989337#post989337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a note, Lunar Exalted ARE Celestial Exalted. So by the metaphysics implied by the setting, the guy who stuffs one and uses it as a display piece is... having a bad time.<br /> <br /> When you kill any Celestial, what you do is build them a nice, proper tomb, throw them a lavish funeral, and bury them will full honors. You do this because Celestial ghosts are known to be very, very uppity.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;And this is the pride of my ancestors - a taxidermied war form Lunar!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...I only see a giant block of salt.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, well, in order to safely keep it, it turns out that you have to make sure that the hungry ghost that's inside never gets out. So, it's encased in a block of rock salt. But it's totally there!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure. Just like that moonsilver axe that's not on the wall.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What are you talking about? I just put it back.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;...Uh oh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:04:33-07:00","id":989477,"title":"","content":"If there's something in the game that is so rigid that it keeps me from having characters who can mutilate or defile the remains of their enemies for trophies, then that thing is wrong.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm pretty sure I once read a reference to some guy keeping gilded skulls of Dragon Blooded on his desk; is he constantly worried about ghosts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T12:32:55-07:00","id":989488,"title":"","content":"Tbh, if you're powerful enough to kill a Lunar, you're probably powerful enough to kill a Lunar's hungry ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:03:48-07:00","id":989496,"title":"","content":"Or to just bribe a Sijanese funerist to do a less-than-respectful exorcism on the DL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T13:52:33-07:00","id":989517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>whimsicalpigeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989477#post989477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If there's something in the game that is so rigid that it keeps me from having characters who can mutilate or defile the remains of their enemies for trophies, then that thing is wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not that it <i><b>stops</b></i> you. It's just that killing people has consequences. And one of those consequences is the reason the elder Solars all got kickass tombs! Elder Lunars killed in the Usurpation ought to have had them, too. Whether your PC wants to bother, well... it's your choice.<br /> <br /> Also, if you are a specialized murderhobo, you can probably fight ghosts too, like Anubis said. Personally, I suspect that the ghosts of young Celestials are no more terrifying than Dragon-Blooded ghosts. Which is still scary, but not &quot;Oh God I Made Another Deathlord&quot; scary. [/silly hyperbole]<br /> <br /> Fighting off the angry reincarnation who brings a bunch of friends and ambushes you in your sleep, that's another challenge.<br /> <br /> Also if you commit genocide, or torture mortals to death, you can get ghosts. Which generally aren't as scary as ghosts of Exalted, but still a consequence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":896,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","user":"Erinys","date":". 10-18-2016, 04:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:39:43-07:00","id":989542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989517#post989517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not that it <i><b>stops</b></i> you.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bPresents an obstacle or incentive against, then.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just that killing people has consequences.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWell, sometimes it does. Sometimes a person is murdered and their body dumped, and that's the end of them in every respect. That guy from the fiction book that the gambling god saved, there probably wouldn't have been any consequences if he'd been killed.<br /> <br /> \u200bI've read some descriptions of the Wild Hunt that make it sound like this. Some young Solar or Lunar, alone and friendless, chased down by motivated people conditioned against hesitation and remorse. That sounds like a formula for somebody dying unknown, unremembered and unmourned.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one of those consequences is the reason the elder Solars all got kickass tombs! Elder Lunars killed in the Usurpation ought to have had them, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>So make trophies out of younger Exalted, I guess.<br /> <br /> Whether your PC wants to bother, well... it's your choice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fighting off the angry reincarnation who brings a bunch of friends and ambushes you in your sleep, that's another challenge.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhat are they so angry about?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also if you commit genocide, or torture mortals to death, you can get ghosts. Which generally aren't as scary as ghosts of Exalted, but still a consequence.</div> </div> </div> </div>But can they get out of the Underworld?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12512-whimsicalpigeon","name":"whimsicalpigeon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T14:52:21-07:00","id":989554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>whimsicalpigeon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989542#post989542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bWhat are they so angry about?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Wyld Hunt who have been genocidally hunting down their kind for a thousand years, and perhaps terrorizing them personally. The particular Wyld Hunt who they personally remember brutally murdering them or possibly torturing them to death. What Lunar <i><b>wouldn't</b></i> be angry?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">She/Her. I am literal-minded and write literally. If I don't say something explicitly, please never assume I implied it. The only exception is if I try to make a joke.</span></span></span></div> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">My point of view may be different from yours but is equally valid.</span></span></span><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/1x1ycoxJF0G9niMt5D3Pp7owZ7tw8AJvL?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted-cWoD-ArM url mega-library</a>. Exalted <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/663334-random-name-generator\" target=\"_blank\">name-generators</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/896-erinys","name":"Erinys","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar896_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4235"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T15:15:08-07:00","id":989567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Piff</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989337#post989337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a note, Lunar Exalted ARE Celestial Exalted. So by the metaphysics implied by the setting, the guy who stuffs one and uses it as a display piece is... having a bad time.<br /> <br /> When you kill any Celestial, what you do is build them a nice, proper tomb, throw them a lavish funeral, and bury them will full honors. You do this because Celestial ghosts are known to be very, very uppity.</div> </div> </div> </div>A kill so nice, I hunted it twice! Actually, that's a great reason to maintain the remains of vanquished foes. You can use their angry ghosts to train new recruits!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-18T17:05:52-07:00","id":989622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketrus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989567#post989567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A kill so nice, I hunted it twice! Actually, that's a great reason to maintain the remains of vanquished foes. You can use their angry ghosts to train new recruits!</div> </div> </div> </div>If hungry ghost stats are anything like they were in prior editions, that probably wouldn't be such a good idea. Their Strength ratings were through the roof, and their damage even more so, since you got +1 Strength <u><b>and</b></u> +3L claw damage for every dot of Essence the Exalt had in life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T01:30:59-07:00","id":989774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Erinys</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/981208-do-lunars-have-any-ancient-artifacts?p=989391#post989391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is <a href=\"http://rathess.xi.co.nz/exalted/index.php/Artifacts:Quagmire_Perimeter_Mine\" target=\"_blank\">a canon trap similar to that</a>, in jade. Apparently runs on an Essence battery which seems weird to me, but I guess that saves on having to keep it attuned indefinitely. How did you envision your moonsilver traps being &quot;powered&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The moonsilver traps for maximum effect would need to be attuned, this primes the trap. The trap would go dormant if the attunement was released. This allows a &quot;minefield&quot; effect without a host of essencce batteries and other arcane means. Again I have not really sat down and played with the idea.<br /> Given the scope of workings in the new edition, something that sadly I just have not had a lot of time to devote reading up on. I would think certain previous artifact effects could be replaced by workings. Perhaps in this edition instead of moonsilver traps as a defense I would use a working to achieve similar effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}